/* The 365 whispers (daily cards, a year without a repeat), shared by the app and the server:
   [id, title, symbol, message, reflection, art motif, painting]. The first 100 have their own paintings; the others
   name the card whose painting they share (and carry its motif).
   Classic script so the browser can load it directly; lib/art.mjs imports it for the same list. */
globalThis.KOSMIA_WHISPERS=[
 ["open-path", "The Open Path", "path", "The path has not closed; it is gathering itself beneath your feet. What feels like waiting is the old magic of becoming, and it is almost done.", "If the waiting is itself part of the becoming, what might you be missing by treating this moment only as a delay?", "a winding path climbing gently through hills toward a single bright star"],
 ["quiet-moon", "The Quiet Moon", "moon", "The Moon hides her face and loses nothing of her power. In your dark phase, something luminous is being restored.", "Who taught you that your worth is measured by your output, and do you still believe them?", "a slender crescent moon resting in a hush of dark-blue night and soft clouds"],
 ["rising-sun", "The Rising Sun", "sun", "Dawn does not ask the night for permission. The first step is already lit; the rest of the road will rise to meet you.", "What would you dare to begin if you no longer needed certainty about where it ends?", "a sun just clearing the horizon, long rays fanning over a still sea"],
 ["steady-star", "The Steady Star", "star", "Long before you were born, a star was set to guide you. It still burns. Steer by it, and the sky will make way.", "Where have you been spending your strength trying to control the sky, instead of learning to steer by it?", "a four-pointed guiding star above a small boat on calm water"],
 ["inner-key", "The Inner Key", "key", "The key you seek has been warm in your own palm all along. In stillness, the lock reveals itself.", "What do you already know, deep down, that you keep waiting for someone else to confirm?", "an ornate antique key held in open cupped hands, glowing softly"],
 ["late-bloom", "The Late Bloom", "flower", "Your bloom was written in a slower, deeper season. When it opens, it will open for good.", "If no one else’s garden existed, how would you judge the pace of your own growth?", "a single flower opening in an autumn garden while other stems rest"],
 ["watchful-eye", "The Watchful Eye", "eye", "An unseen eye watches over you with love. What keeps returning is a sign; follow it, and a door will open.", "What keeps returning to your life, and what might it be asking you to finally understand?", "a serene open eye framed by a crescent and scattered stars"],
 ["distant-ship", "The Distant Ship", "ship", "What sails away is carrying a message to your future. The harbour you are meant for is already lighting its lamps.", "What departure that once felt like loss has quietly carried you somewhere you needed to be?", "a sailing ship far out on the horizon heading toward a lit harbour"],
 ["old-tree", "The Old Tree", "tree", "Beneath the silence, your roots have reached ancient water. Soon the branches will show what the dark has made.", "Which part of your work matters most precisely because no one will ever see it?", "an ancient tree with deep roots visible beneath the earth, stars in its branches"],
 ["turning-wheel", "The Turning Wheel", "wheel", "The wheel is turning in your favour. What falls away now clears the ground for what is destined to arrive.", "If you cannot choose the season, what would it mean to live this one fully rather than wait for the next?", "a wheel of the four seasons, spring blossom to winter frost around its rim"],
 ["white-lily", "The White Lily", "lily", "The lily opens without force, and the whole garden turns towards her. Your softness is a power the world has been waiting for.", "Whose voice do you hear when you speak to yourself harshly, and is it really yours?", "a white lily in soft moonlight with dew on its petals"],
 ["clear-crystal", "The Clear Crystal", "crystal", "Truth is crystallising inside you, facet by facet. Soon you will see through what once clouded everything.", "What truth about your life have you been avoiding, and what might become clear if you stopped?", "a faceted quartz crystal catching starlight and splitting it into soft colour"],
 ["first-light", "The First Light", "sun", "A spark has been placed in your keeping. Guard it tenderly; it carries the fire of a life still unwritten.", "Why do we so often dismiss beginnings for being small, when everything great began that way?", "a single candle flame glowing at dawn"],
 ["silver-thread", "The Silver Thread", "moon", "An invisible thread binds you to souls you have not yet met. Pull it gently today, and someone, somewhere, will feel it.", "If every kindness travels further than you can see, what are you sending out into the world today?", "a silver thread linking two distant lanterns across the night"],
 ["still-water", "The Still Water", "lily", "Be still, and the deep will speak. What rises to your surface now is a gift from the depths of your own soul.", "What do you lose by never letting your mind fall quiet enough to see its own depths?", "a mirror-still lake reflecting the moon"],
 ["open-door", "The Open Door", "key", "A door has opened where you did not expect one. Light spills through it; you have only to look, and you will know.", "Is it fear of what lies beyond the door, or fear of who you might become there, that keeps you from looking?", "an ancient arched door standing ajar with light beyond"],
 ["gentle-rain", "The Gentle Rain", "flower", "This rain is not a sorrow but a blessing in disguise. Where it falls, the ground of your life grows soft enough for miracles.", "Can you recall a difficult season that later revealed itself as the soil for something good?", "soft rain falling on a blossoming garden"],
 ["north-star", "The North Star", "star", "Your North Star has never moved. When the night is wide and unclear, turn your face to it and you are home.", "When everything around you shifts, what is the one value you would refuse to give up?", "the pole star shining above a lone traveller on a path"],
 ["quiet-harvest", "The Quiet Harvest", "tree", "The harvest is greater than you know. Count your blessings, and they will quietly multiply.", "What would change if you measured your life by what you have gathered rather than by what you still lack?", "golden wheat sheaves under a harvest moon"],
 ["hidden-garden", "The Hidden Garden", "flower", "There is a secret garden in you that only you can enter. Tend it today; its flowers carry your true name.", "What part of you exists only in private, and does it receive the same care you give your public self?", "a walled garden glimpsed through an ivy-covered gate"],
 ["the-bridge", "The Bridge", "path", "A bridge is forming beneath your feet with every brave choice. The far shore is closer than the mist would have you believe.", "What is the smallest honest step toward the person you hope to become?", "a stone bridge arching over a misty river"],
 ["the-lantern", "The Lantern", "sun", "You carry a flame the dark cannot touch. Hold it high enough for the next step, and the path will reveal itself.", "Why do we feel we must solve everything at once, when life only ever asks for the next step?", "a lantern held aloft in a dark forest"],
 ["wild-horse", "The Wild Horse", "path", "A wild, untamed spirit runs beside you. Loosen the reins today; it knows the way to your joy.", "Which rules you live by did you choose, and which did you simply inherit?", "a wild horse galloping across moonlit plains"],
 ["golden-hour", "The Golden Hour", "sun", "The light is turning gold for you. Look up: this hour was made to remind you how beautiful your life already is.", "If beauty only ever arrives in passing, what would it mean to live in a way that notices it?", "a sunset bathing rolling hills in gold"],
 ["deep-roots", "The Deep Roots", "tree", "Storms come to show the strength of the roots. Yours run deeper than any wind; you will stand.", "What holds you steady when everything else shakes, and have you thanked it lately?", "a great oak holding fast in a gale"],
 ["returning-tide", "The Returning Tide", "ship", "The tide always remembers its shore. What belongs to you is already finding its way back.", "Can you love something without needing it to return, and still leave room for it to come back?", "the tide rolling back over a moonlit beach"],
 ["the-mirror", "The Mirror", "eye", "The mirror shows you a truth the world cannot. Look with kind eyes, and you will meet a self you can love.", "What does your strongest reaction to someone else reveal about what you have not yet accepted in yourself?", "an ornate hand mirror reflecting a starry sky"],
 ["the-feather", "The Feather", "lily", "A feather drifts down to remind you: you were never meant to carry it all. Let the air hold you a while.", "What are you carrying out of habit rather than necessity, and what would happen if you set it down?", "a single feather drifting on a breeze"],
 ["the-spiral", "The Spiral", "wheel", "You are not walking in circles; you are ascending. Each familiar lesson now meets a wiser, stronger you.", "What lesson keeps finding you, and how has the way you meet it changed since the last time?", "a spiral staircase climbing towards the stars"],
 ["the-ember", "The Ember", "sun", "The fire was never out. Beneath the ash an ember waits for your breath, ready to blaze again.", "What did you once love so fiercely that part of it still glows in you, waiting?", "glowing embers in an old stone hearth"],
 ["the-compass", "The Compass", "star", "Your inner compass whispers beneath the world's noise, and it has never pointed you wrong. Listen, and go.", "If you silenced every outside opinion for one day, which direction would you walk?", "a brass compass resting on an old map"],
 ["nightingale", "The Nightingale", "moon", "Sing, even into the silence. Your voice is a spell, and the night is listening.", "What would you create, say or become if no one were ever going to applaud it?", "a nightingale singing on a moonlit branch"],
 ["crossroads", "The Crossroads", "path", "Every road at this crossing hides a gift. The one that makes your heart quicken is the one that is yours.", "If every path teaches you something, what makes one path truly yours?", "a weathered signpost where three country roads meet"],
 ["sanctuary", "The Sanctuary", "lily", "A sanctuary waits inside you, older than any worry. Step in; nothing there asks you to be anything but whole.", "Why does rest so often feel like something we must earn, rather than something we are allowed?", "a candlelit stone chapel with open arched windows"],
 ["butterfly", "The Butterfly", "flower", "You are not falling apart; you are taking flight. The cocoon is only the beginning of your wings.", "What part of you is falling apart so that something truer can take its place?", "a butterfly emerging from its chrysalis"],
 ["lighthouse", "The Lighthouse", "star", "You were made to be a light for others. Stand firm where you are, and ships you will never see find their way by you.", "How can you be a light for others without abandoning the ground you stand on?", "a lighthouse beam sweeping over a stormy sea"],
 ["the-seed", "The Seed", "tree", "Plant your hope today and trust the earth with it. Hidden things grow fastest in the dark.", "What would you plant today if you trusted that its growth did not depend on your watching it?", "a seedling sprouting from dark rich soil"],
 ["two-moons", "The Two Moons", "moon", "Two moons rise in your sky: what you have lost and what is coming. You are vast enough to hold them both.", "Which two opposing truths are you holding right now, and what if neither had to win?", "two moons rising side by side over the sea"],
 ["the-weaver", "The Weaver", "wheel", "An unseen hand weaves your days into a pattern of rare beauty. Every thread, even the dark ones, has its place.", "If today were the only thread you could add to your life’s tapestry, how would you want it to look?", "a loom weaving golden threads into a tapestry of stars"],
 ["the-mountain", "The Mountain", "path", "The mountain bows to those who climb it. Look back: you have already risen higher than you thought you could.", "If you never reached the summit, would the climb still have been worth it?", "a winding trail up a mountain beneath the stars"],
 ["the-owl", "The Owl", "eye", "The owl sees what daylight hides. Tonight, wisdom will come to you as a quiet knowing; trust it.", "What do you know at night, in the quiet, that you forget to honour by day?", "an owl perched on an ancient tree at night"],
 ["golden-key", "The Golden Key", "key", "A golden key has been placed in your path. The simplest door is the one that opens.", "Why do we so often distrust the simple answer, as if difficulty were proof of truth?", "a golden key glowing on a velvet cushion"],
 ["the-river", "The River", "ship", "Stop swimming against the current. The river knows where your joy is waiting, and it is carrying you there.", "Where in your life are you pushing against a current that might carry you if you let it?", "a river winding through a moonlit valley"],
 ["the-phoenix", "The Phoenix", "sun", "What burned was only the old skin. From these ashes you rise brighter, fiercer and entirely your own.", "What ending in your life made room for a beginning you could not have imagined at the time?", "a phoenix rising in gold and flame"],
 ["the-lotus", "The Lotus", "lily", "The lotus rises from the mud untouched. Nothing you have walked through has been wasted; it has made you bloom.", "What has your hardest experience given you that an easier life never could?", "a lotus blooming from a dark pond"],
 ["stargazer", "The Stargazer", "star", "The stars are leaning closer to hear your dreams. Dream them larger; the sky has room for every one.", "What dream have you made smaller in order to make it seem possible?", "a figure gazing at the heavens through a brass telescope"],
 ["the-hearth", "The Hearth", "sun", "Your warmth is a hearth others gather around without knowing why. Tend it, and home will follow you everywhere.", "Who feels at home in your presence, and what is it that you offer them?", "a glowing hearth with a teapot and a sleeping cat"],
 ["the-wind", "The Wind", "path", "A wind of change is rising just for you. Open your sails; it is carrying you towards something new.", "What change are you resisting that might, if welcomed, carry you forward?", "wind filling the sails of a small boat"],
 ["the-fox", "The Fox", "eye", "The fox moves with quiet cunning and wastes nothing. Guard your fire today; spend it only where it multiplies.", "Which battles in your life are truly yours to fight, and which have you simply been drawn into?", "a fox watching quietly from tall grass at dusk"],
 ["the-chalice", "The Chalice", "crystal", "Your heart is a sacred cup. Fill it first, and what overflows will bless everyone near you.", "What does it look like to care for yourself as faithfully as you care for others?", "a golden chalice overflowing with starlight"],
 ["the-eclipse", "The Eclipse", "moon", "The light is not lost, only veiled for a moment. When this eclipse passes, you will shine with something new.", "If this darkness is only passing, what light in you is it waiting to reveal again?", "a solar eclipse with a glowing corona"],
 ["the-tapestry", "The Tapestry", "wheel", "You are a tapestry still on the loom. One dark thread is part of a pattern more beautiful than you can yet see.", "Which single moment have you allowed to define your whole story, and is that fair to you?", "an unfinished tapestry on an old wooden loom"],
 ["the-blossom", "The Blossom", "flower", "Joy is blossoming without asking permission. Let it in; it was sent to find you.", "When did you last let yourself feel joy without needing a reason to deserve it?", "cherry blossoms drifting in spring light"],
 ["sacred-flame", "The Sacred Flame", "crystal", "There is a flame in you that is holy. Shelter it from the wind, and it will light your whole life.", "What do you hold sacred, and how well are you protecting it from the winds of the everyday?", "a flame burning inside a crystal lantern"],
 ["dawn-chorus", "The Dawn Chorus", "sun", "The world is reborn at every dawn, and so are you. The morning chorus is singing your name.", "If you could begin again this morning, what would you choose to leave behind in yesterday?", "birds singing in the trees as dawn breaks"],
 ["the-anchor", "The Anchor", "ship", "You belong somewhere, and the anchor remembers where. Staying can be its own quiet act of courage.", "What in your life is asking you to stay a little longer, rather than drift towards whatever comes next?", "an old iron anchor resting on a sandy seabed among swaying kelp"],
 ["the-hourglass", "The Hourglass", "wheel", "Time is not slipping away from you; it is pouring into you. Every grain becomes the wisdom you carry.", "If you saw your days as lived rather than spent, how might you feel about the ones behind you?", "an antique hourglass on a wooden desk, sand falling in a thin bright stream"],
 ["the-stile", "The Stile", "path", "You stand on a threshold between two worlds. Pause; the step that is yours will feel like coming home.", "What changes when you allow yourself to linger in between, rather than rushing to arrive?", "a worn wooden stile set in a dry-stone wall between two misty fields"],
 ["the-well", "The Well", "crystal", "You drink from a well dug by those who loved you before you were born. Draw deeply; there is more than enough.", "What have you inherited from those who came before you that you wish to pass on, and what would you rather let settle?", "a moss-covered stone well with a wooden bucket hanging from its rope"],
 ["the-bell", "The Bell", "eye", "A bell is ringing in the quiet, meant for your ears alone. Listen until its last note, and the answer will be there.", "When did you last listen to someone without already preparing your reply?", "a bronze bell hanging in an open stone belfry beneath the stars"],
 ["the-nest", "The Nest", "tree", "Your nest is woven from small, faithful things. Each one you gather today makes your shelter stronger.", "What small, ordinary thing could you add today to the place where you feel safe?", "a woven bird’s nest holding three speckled eggs in a forked branch"],
 ["the-snail", "The Snail", "path", "The snail carries its home and arrives exactly on time. Your pace is sacred; you will arrive.", "What would you notice along the way if you allowed yourself to travel at your own pace?", "a snail with a spiral shell climbing a dewy fern frond"],
 ["the-kite", "The Kite", "sun", "Let something lift you without reason. The wind loves a soul that still remembers how to play.", "When did you last do something purely for the joy of it, with no purpose at all?", "a diamond-shaped kite with a ribboned tail flying high above a windy meadow"],
 ["the-moth", "The Moth", "moon", "The moth flies towards the light it cannot explain. Your longing is a map; follow where it glows.", "What keeps drawing you towards it, and what might it be trying to show you?", "a pale moth with long trailing wings resting on a birch branch under the moon"],
 ["the-hive", "The Hive", "flower", "The hive hums with shared sweetness. Let others carry some of the work, and taste what you make together.", "Who might you let help you, if you stopped believing you had to do it all yourself?", "an old straw beehive skep in a meadow, bees drifting among the clover"],
 ["the-willow", "The Willow", "tree", "The willow bows to the storm and greets the dawn unbroken. Bending is a secret kind of strength.", "Where might softening, rather than resisting, help you come through this season?", "a weeping willow trailing its long branches into a quiet stream"],
 ["the-sundial", "The Sundial", "sun", "Every hour of your life counts, the shaded and the bright. Even the shadows are telling the time of your becoming.", "Which hours of your life do you discount, and what might they have been quietly teaching you?", "a weathered stone sundial in a summer garden, its shadow falling across its face"],
 ["the-harp", "The Harp", "star", "A string in you is answering a song from far away. Listen: something kindred is calling your name.", "What in the world around you stirs something in you that you rarely give voice to?", "an old wooden harp standing alone in a sunlit room"],
 ["snow-tracks", "The Snow Tracks", "path", "In the snow, your own footsteps finally speak. Solitude is where your soul hears itself clearly.", "What do you discover about yourself when no one else is there to reflect you back?", "a single trail of footprints crossing a fresh snowfield under a pale winter sky"],
 ["the-hare", "The Hare", "moon", "Wonder is the swift hare at the edge of the field. Leave a gap in your day, and it will leap through.", "What ordinary thing would astonish you if you were seeing it for the very first time?", "a hare leaping over a frosted hillside beneath a full moon"],
 ["the-heron", "The Heron", "eye", "The heron waits, perfectly still, and never misses its moment. Yours is coming; you will know it when it arrives.", "What moment are you trying to force that might simply need you to wait and watch?", "a grey heron standing on one leg in the shallows of a reed-fringed pool"],
 ["the-scales", "The Scales", "wheel", "Balance is a dance, not a destination. Every small adjustment brings you closer to your centre.", "What small adjustment could bring today a little closer to balance?", "a pair of brass balance scales holding a rose petal and a pebble"],
 ["the-labyrinth", "The Labyrinth", "path", "The labyrinth turns back on itself, yet it always leads to the heart. You are on the right path, even now.", "Where might what feels like going backwards actually be part of the way through?", "a turf labyrinth cut into a green hillside, seen from above at dusk"],
 ["the-swing", "The Swing", "sun", "The child you once were still holds the map to your joy. Take their hand today and remember what you love.", "What did you love as a child that you set down when you learned to be careful?", "a wooden rope swing hanging from a high bough over a summer meadow"],
 ["stepping-stones", "The Stepping Stones", "path", "Courage often arrives disguised as a trembling step. Take it; the stones are already rising beneath your feet.", "What would you attempt if you did not have to feel brave first?", "flat stepping stones crossing a shallow, rushing stream"],
 ["the-birdcage", "The Birdcage", "key", "The cage door has been open all along. Lean into the latch and step into the sky you were born for.", "Which limits you live within were once necessary, and are they still?", "an open ornate birdcage with a small bird perched on its threshold"],
 ["sealed-letter", "The Sealed Letter", "lily", "A letter of forgiveness, written and never sent, can still set a soul free. Write it, and feel the lock turn.", "Who, including yourself, might you begin to forgive without needing them to know?", "a folded letter sealed with red wax beside a quill and inkwell"],
 ["the-orchard", "The Orchard", "tree", "What you plant today will feed hearts you will never meet. Your kindness grows orchards across time.", "What are you tending now that might nourish someone long after you have moved on?", "a wicker basket of rosy apples beneath a laden orchard bough"],
 ["the-comet", "The Comet", "star", "A comet crosses your sky only once. Be present for the wonder; you do not need to understand it to be changed.", "What rare thing is passing through your life now that you might be too busy to look up for?", "a comet with a long luminous tail streaking above a sleeping village"],
 ["the-aurora", "The Aurora", "star", "Your darkest night holds colours you have not yet seen. The aurora is already beginning to dance.", "What colours might be hidden in the night you are moving through now?", "curtains of the northern lights rippling over a snowy pine forest"],
 ["the-waterfall", "The Waterfall", "ship", "Let it fall like a waterfall: loud, shining and free. In the release, you will find a rainbow.", "What feeling have you been keeping tidy that might need to fall freely for a while?", "a tall waterfall pouring into a fern-lined pool"],
 ["the-snowdrop", "The Snowdrop", "flower", "The snowdrop rises before the frost has gone. Your hope is stronger than any winter.", "What small sign of returning warmth have you overlooked because winter is not quite over?", "snowdrops pushing up through a thin layer of late snow"],
 ["the-cairn", "The Cairn", "path", "A small stone placed with love marks your way home. Build your ritual, and it will always lead you back to yourself.", "What small daily act steadies you, and how might you honour it a little more?", "a cairn of balanced stones on a windswept moorland ridge"],
 ["the-hedgerow", "The Hedgerow", "tree", "The hedgerow shelters life on both its sides. Your boundaries are a living blessing, not a wall.", "Where would a gentle boundary protect what you love without shutting anyone out?", "a flowering hawthorn hedgerow alive with small birds along a country lane"],
 ["the-web", "The Web", "crystal", "What was torn can be woven again, more beautifully than before. The spider begins each dawn without bitterness, and so can you.", "What might you rebuild if you let go of your resentment that it ever fell?", "a spider’s web strung with dewdrops in early morning sunlight"],
 ["the-balloon", "The Balloon", "sun", "Rise above the day for a moment. From up here, every knot is smaller, and the way ahead is plain.", "How might today’s trouble look from a year from now, or from high above?", "a striped hot-air balloon drifting over a patchwork of fields"],
 ["the-kingfisher", "The Kingfisher", "eye", "The kingfisher strikes true because it sees only one thing. Give your heart to one purpose today, and it will flash gold.", "What might change if you gave one task today your whole, undivided attention?", "a kingfisher perched on a reed above a clear brook"],
 ["the-stag", "The Stag", "tree", "You are the stag in the clearing, crowned and unafraid. Take your space; the forest makes way for you.", "Where do you make yourself smaller than you are, and whose comfort is it really for?", "a stag with branching antlers standing in a misty forest clearing"],
 ["the-whale", "The Whale", "ship", "Your grief is love singing in deep water. Let it travel through you; it will carry you somewhere gentler.", "What would it mean to let your grief be a measure of your love rather than a problem to solve?", "a great whale gliding through deep blue water beneath shafts of light"],
 ["the-swan", "The Swan", "lily", "Grace glides on the surface, and strength moves beneath. You are more powerful than anyone can see.", "What hidden effort in your own life deserves more recognition than you give it?", "a white swan gliding across a misty pond at dawn"],
 ["the-pomegranate", "The Pomegranate", "crystal", "You hold a hundred seeds of possibility. Every version of you has a gift to give; let them all be welcome.", "Which part of you rarely gets a say, and what would it tell you if it did?", "a pomegranate split open to reveal its jewelled seeds on a pewter plate"],
 ["daily-bread", "The Daily Bread", "sun", "What you need for today has already been given. Notice it, and enough becomes abundance.", "What would it feel like to say ‘this is enough’ and mean it, even for one day?", "a fresh loaf of bread cooling on a wooden table beside a jug of milk"],
 ["the-pinecone", "The Pine Cone", "tree", "The pine cone opens only when the fire has come. Your season of opening is near; you are ready.", "What in you has been waiting for the right conditions, and might those conditions be arriving now?", "a pine cone opening its scales on a bed of forest moss"],
 ["the-nautilus", "The Nautilus", "wheel", "You have outgrown the old rooms of your life. Each chamber you leave behind still lifts you higher.", "What part of your past self are you ready to thank and move beyond?", "a cross-section of a nautilus shell showing its spiralling chambers"],
 ["the-dandelion", "The Dandelion", "flower", "Make a wish and let it fly. The wind knows exactly where to plant it.", "What hope are you holding so tightly that it has no room to travel?", "a dandelion clock releasing its seeds into a summer breeze"],
 ["music-box", "The Music Box", "wheel", "An old song is playing in a new key. You are free to let your memories become gentle again.", "Which memory might you hear differently now that you are no longer who you were then?", "an open music box with a tiny turning swan and a brass comb"],
 ["wild-geese", "The Wild Geese", "ship", "The geese leave without guilt and return without shame. Trust the season that is calling you onwards.", "What would change if you let your comings and goings be seasonal rather than failures?", "a skein of wild geese flying in a long V over autumn fields at dusk"],
 ["fairy-ring", "The Fairy Ring", "moon", "Unseen threads connect you beneath the surface of things. You are held by more than you know.", "Who quietly holds you up in ways you rarely see or acknowledge?", "a ring of mushrooms in a mossy woodland glade by moonlight"],
 ["the-frost", "The Frost", "crystal", "The frost paints a new pattern every night and lets it go by noon. Release yesterday's certainties; tomorrow's are more beautiful.", "Which belief have you held so long that you have stopped checking whether it is still true?", "delicate frost ferns spreading across a cottage window pane"],
 ["the-bench", "The Bench", "moon", "The simple hours you share with those you love are secretly sacred. Keep turning up; this is where magic lives.", "Which friend have you been meaning to reach for, and what small gesture might bring you closer again?", "a weathered wooden bench for two beneath a flowering lime tree at evening"],
 ["the-thaw","The Thaw","crystal","Listen: the ice is beginning to speak in drips and whispers. What froze in you is not lost, only resting, and it is already softening towards the light.","What in you has been frozen for safety, and what gentle warmth might it be ready to receive now?","snowdrops pushing up through a thin layer of late snow","the-snowdrop"],
 ["rock-pool","The Rock Pool","ship","When the sea draws back, a small world is left shining in the stone. Look closely at what remains with you; it is fuller of life than you imagined.","When something larger withdrew from your life, what small and living thing did it leave behind for you to find?","the tide rolling back over a moonlit beach","returning-tide"],
 ["the-swallow","The Swallow","ship","The swallow crosses deserts and seas to find the same old barn again. Something in you knows the way back to where you belong, however far you roam.","Which place, person or practice do you keep finding your way back to, and what does it give you?","a skein of wild geese flying in a long V over autumn fields at dusk","wild-geese"],
 ["the-robin","The Robin","sun","The robin sings through the coldest months as if spring were already promised. Let your own small song carry warmth into a season that has forgotten it.","Who in your life might need a little warmth from you while their own season is cold?","a flowering hawthorn hedgerow alive with small birds along a country lane","the-hedgerow"],
 ["the-acorn","The Acorn","tree","An entire oak sleeps inside a shell you could hold in your palm. Do not judge your beginnings by their size; a whole forest is folded inside you.","What small beginning in your life are you underestimating simply because it does not yet look like much?","a great oak holding fast in a gale","deep-roots"],
 ["fallow-field","The Fallow Field","path","The field that rests this year will feed the village the next. Your stillness is not idleness; the earth of you is gathering its quiet strength.","What would it mean to let one part of your life lie fallow for a season, without guilt?","golden wheat sheaves under a harvest moon","quiet-harvest"],
 ["soft-moss","The Moss","crystal","Moss asks for nothing but shade and patience, and in time it softens every stone. Your gentleness, given slowly, is reshaping more than you can see.","Where has your quiet persistence softened something hard over the years, even if no one noticed?","a ring of mushrooms in a mossy woodland glade by moonlight","fairy-ring"],
 ["the-fern","The Fern","lily","The fern unfurls one green curl at a time and never hurries. Let today open you only as far as it wishes; the rest will come in its season.","Which part of you is unfurling right now, and how could you give it more room and less hurry?","a tall waterfall pouring into a fern-lined pool","the-waterfall"],
 ["morning-mist","The Morning Mist","eye","The mist hides the valley only until the sun is high enough. What is unclear to you now is not missing; it is simply waiting to be revealed.","What are you trying to see clearly before its time, and what might patience show you instead?","a stone bridge arching over a misty river","the-bridge"],
 ["distant-thunder","The Distant Thunder","key","Thunder rolls over the hills, and behind it the air grows sweet and clean. Even the loudest disturbance in your life is clearing the way for something fresh.","What recent upheaval might, in time, prove to have cleared the air in your life?","a lighthouse beam sweeping over a stormy sea","lighthouse"],
 ["the-rainbow","The Rainbow","crystal","Light needs the rain to show you all its colours. Your tears and your sunlight together are painting something luminous across the sky of your life.","What beauty in you could only have appeared because both sorrow and light passed through you?","soft rain falling on a blossoming garden","gentle-rain"],
 ["the-estuary","The Estuary","ship","Here the river meets the sea and becomes something larger without ceasing to be itself. You are allowed to grow wide and still remain wholly you.","Where are you afraid that growing larger will cost you who you are, and is that truly so?","a river winding through a moonlit valley","the-river"],
 ["the-brook","The Brook","ship","The brook sings because of the stones in its way, not in spite of them. Your obstacles are quietly giving your life its own particular music.","Which obstacle in your life has, without your noticing, given you a voice or a gift you value?","flat stepping stones crossing a shallow, rushing stream","stepping-stones"],
 ["high-pass","The High Pass","path","Between two peaks the old road threads its narrow way. You need not conquer the mountain today; only find the gentle pass already waiting for you.","Where are you trying to climb straight over something when a gentler way around might already exist?","a winding trail up a mountain beneath the stars","the-mountain"],
 ["the-badger","The Badger","moon","The badger keeps its ancient paths by night, faithful to the same old ways. There is strength in your steady habits; they are carving a road your soul can trust.","Which of your quiet, faithful habits has been holding you together more than you give it credit for?","a fox watching quietly from tall grass at dusk","the-fox"],
 ["bluebell-wood","The Bluebell Wood","flower","For a few weeks the woodland floor becomes a sea of blue, then sleeps again. Some joys are brief by design; meet them fully while they bloom.","Which brief joy in your life right now deserves your full attention before its season passes?","cherry blossoms drifting in spring light","the-blossom"],
 ["the-bramble","The Bramble","key","The bramble that catches your sleeve also offers the sweetest fruit in the hedge. What has pricked you may yet hold something worth gathering.","What difficult person or situation might be offering you something sweet beneath its thorns?","a flowering hawthorn hedgerow alive with small birds along a country lane","the-hedgerow"],
 ["the-hazel","The Hazel","tree","In the old tales the hazel holds the nuts of wisdom, ripening slowly beside the pool. Your understanding is ripening too; let it fall when it is ready.","What understanding about your life feels almost ripe, and what would help it fall gently into your hands?","a seedling sprouting from dark rich soil","the-seed"],
 ["the-furrow","The Furrow","path","The plough turns the earth so that light can reach what was buried. Being turned over is not ruin; it is how new ground is made ready.","What upheaval in your life might be turning over old ground so that something new can grow?","a seedling sprouting from dark rich soil","the-seed"],
 ["the-equinox","The Equinox","wheel","Today the light and the dark stand in perfect measure, and neither one wins. You, too, can hold both within you without having to choose between them.","Where in your life are light and dark asking to be held in balance rather than resolved?","a wheel of the four seasons, spring blossom to winter frost around its rim","turning-wheel"],
 ["the-solstice","The Solstice","sun","At the year’s deepest turning, the sun pauses and begins its slow return. Whatever you are passing through, the light has already started coming back to you.","What sign, however faint, tells you that the light is beginning to return to your life?","a sun just clearing the horizon, long rays fanning over a still sea","rising-sun"],
 ["longest-night","The Longest Night","star","The longest night is also the night the stars are most generous. Rest in the dark a while; it is holding more wonder than the day ever could.","What has a long, dark season in your life shown you that brighter days never could?","a slender crescent moon resting in a hush of dark-blue night and soft clouds","quiet-moon"],
 ["the-murmuration","The Murmuration","wheel","Thousands of starlings move as one, each following only its nearest neighbours. Turn gently with those beside you, and you become part of something breathtaking.","Who are the few people nearest to you that shape how you move through the world, and do they lift you?","a skein of wild geese flying in a long V over autumn fields at dusk","wild-geese"],
 ["the-salmon","The Salmon","ship","The salmon leaps upstream, called home by a memory written in its blood. Trust the deep pull you feel; it is leading you back to your source.","What do you feel deeply drawn to return to, even when the current of your life runs the other way?","a river winding through a moonlit valley","the-river"],
 ["the-otter","The Otter","eye","The otter plays in the river and still catches its supper. Lightness and purpose are not enemies; let delight carry you towards what you need.","How might you bring a little more play into the very work you take most seriously?","a kingfisher perched on a reed above a clear brook","the-kingfisher"],
 ["the-honeysuckle","The Honeysuckle","flower","Honeysuckle releases its sweetest scent at dusk, for those who linger. The tenderest gifts of this day are waiting for you to slow down and breathe.","What sweetness in your evenings do you miss because you are still rushing when the day is done?","a weathered wooden bench for two beneath a flowering lime tree at evening","the-bench"],
 ["the-rosehip","The Rose Hip","flower","When the petals have fallen, the rose gives its scarlet fruit to winter. Your endings, too, are bearing a nourishment you could not offer in your bloom.","What has an ending in your life given you that you could not have received while it was still flowering?","a wicker basket of rosy apples beneath a laden orchard bough","the-orchard"],
 ["the-leaf-fall","The Leaf Fall","tree","The tree lets its leaves go in a blaze of colour, without mourning. Release what has served its season, and let the letting go be beautiful.","What could you let go of with grace this season, as a tree releases its leaves in gold?","a wheel of the four seasons, spring blossom to winter frost around its rim","turning-wheel"],
 ["the-tadpole","The Tadpole","lily","The tadpole does not yet know it will leap from the water onto land. You are becoming something your present self cannot imagine; trust the change.","What version of yourself might be forming right now that you cannot yet picture?","a lotus blooming from a dark pond","the-lotus"],
 ["the-dew","The Dew","crystal","Each morning the grass is jewelled with dew that no hand placed there. Grace arrives quietly in the night; wake, and see what has been given.","What gift arrived in your life quietly, without effort, that you have not yet thanked?","a spider’s web strung with dewdrops in early morning sunlight","the-web"],
 ["passing-cloud","The Passing Cloud","sun","Clouds cross the sun but never put it out. Whatever passes over your heart today, the warmth above it is constant, and it will shine on you again.","Which passing mood have you mistaken for the whole weather of your life?","a striped hot-air balloon drifting over a patchwork of fields","the-balloon"],
 ["washed-sky","The Washed Sky","star","After the storm the sky is rinsed so clear that every star returns. What has shaken you has also left you able to see further than before.","After a hard season, what can you now see clearly that was hidden from you before?","a comet with a long luminous tail streaking above a sleeping village","the-comet"],
 ["the-glacier","The Glacier","crystal","The glacier moves too slowly for any eye to see, yet it carves whole valleys. Your patient, steady effort is shaping a landscape that will last.","What slow, faithful effort of yours is changing the shape of your life, though you rarely see it move?","delicate frost ferns spreading across a cottage window pane","the-frost"],
 ["first-snow","The First Snow","lily","The first snow hushes the whole world and makes every path new again. Today you are allowed to begin softly, on a clean white page.","If the world fell silent and every path were new, where would you choose to walk first?","a single trail of footprints crossing a fresh snowfield under a pale winter sky","snow-tracks"],
 ["the-blackbird","The Blackbird","moon","At dusk the blackbird sings from the rooftop as if to bless the ending day. Close your evening with gratitude, and the night will hold you kindly.","What would you like to bless about today before you let it go into the night?","a nightingale singing on a moonlit branch","nightingale"],
 ["the-curlew","The Curlew","eye","The curlew’s call drifts across the moor, wild and full of longing. Your longing is not a weakness; it is the voice of what your soul remembers.","What do you long for that you have never fully admitted, even to yourself?","a cairn of balanced stones on a windswept moorland ridge","the-cairn"],
 ["the-moor","The Moor","path","The open moor hides nothing and asks nothing. Under its wide sky you can set down your guard and simply be as large as you truly are.","Where do you feel free enough to drop every pretence, and how might you go there more often?","a cairn of balanced stones on a windswept moorland ridge","the-cairn"],
 ["the-driftwood","The Driftwood","ship","The driftwood has travelled far and been washed silver by its journey. Where you have wandered has made you beautiful, not lost; the shore is glad of you.","Which of your wanderings, once counted as wasted, has quietly become part of your beauty?","an old iron anchor resting on a sandy seabed among swaying kelp","the-anchor"],
 ["root-cellar","The Root Cellar","key","In the cool dark of the cellar, the harvest is kept safe for the lean months. You have stored more strength than you know; it is there when you need it.","What inner store of strength have you built up over the years that you could draw on now?","a fresh loaf of bread cooling on a wooden table beside a jug of milk","daily-bread"],
 ["the-gleaner","The Gleaner","star","The gleaner walks the field after the harvest and finds it still full of grain. Look again at what you thought was finished; there is more to gather.","What part of your life have you written off as spent, that might still hold something to gather?","golden wheat sheaves under a harvest moon","quiet-harvest"],
 ["the-haymaking","The Haymaking","sun","The long light warms your back while the hay is turned and gathered. This bright season has been given to you for gathering; take it gladly, with both hands.","What is this season of your life asking you to gather while the light is generous?","a sunset bathing rolling hills in gold","golden-hour"],
 ["the-vineyard","The Vineyard","wheel","The vine is pruned hard in winter so that its fruit will be sweeter. What has been cut back in your life is making room for richer gifts.","What has been pruned from your life that may, in time, make the fruit sweeter?","a golden chalice overflowing with starlight","the-chalice"],
 ["the-woodpecker","The Woodpecker","eye","The woodpecker returns to the same tree, knocking until it opens. Keep knocking at the door that matters to you; persistence is its own kind of key.","Which door have you stopped knocking on too soon, and is it worth trying once more?","an owl perched on an ancient tree at night","the-owl"],
 ["the-squirrel","The Squirrel","key","The squirrel buries its treasure all autumn and forgets half of it, and so the forest grows. Not everything you plant needs remembering to flourish.","What have you given or sown and then forgotten, which may still be quietly growing somewhere?","a pine cone opening its scales on a bed of forest moss","the-pinecone"],
 ["the-dragonfly","The Dragonfly","lily","The dragonfly spends years beneath the water before a single summer of flight. Your long, hidden preparation is not wasted; your wings are coming.","What hidden preparation in your life might be leading towards a season of flight?","a mirror-still lake reflecting the moon","still-water"],
 ["evening-primrose","The Evening Primrose","moon","The evening primrose waits for twilight before it opens. You need not bloom on anyone else’s schedule; your own hour has a beauty all its own.","At what hour of the day, or of your life, do you feel most truly yourself?","a white lily in soft moonlight with dew on its petals","white-lily"],
 ["weather-vane","The Weather Vane","wheel","The weather vane turns with every wind, yet it never leaves its roof. You can answer every change and still stay rooted in your own home.","How can you remain open to the winds of change while staying faithful to where you stand?","wind filling the sails of a small boat","the-wind"],
 ["the-saltmarsh","The Saltmarsh","path","The saltmarsh is neither land nor sea, and it teems with life. The in-between places of your life are richer than they appear; walk them with curiosity.","What in-between season are you living through now, and what life might be thriving in it unseen?","a grey heron standing on one leg in the shallows of a reed-fringed pool","the-heron"],
 ["the-puddle","The Puddle","eye","Even a puddle on the lane holds the whole sky. Look down today, and you may find heaven reflected in the humblest places of your life.","Where might you find something vast and beautiful reflected in the most ordinary corner of your day?","an ornate hand mirror reflecting a starry sky","the-mirror"],
 ["rising-sap","The Rising Sap","tree","Unseen beneath the bark, the sap is rising long before the first leaf appears. Something in you is already stirring towards spring; trust it.","What is stirring in you beneath the surface, not yet visible, but already on its way?","a weeping willow trailing its long branches into a quiet stream","the-willow"],
 ["the-dormouse","The Dormouse","moon","The dormouse sleeps through the cold, curled and trusting, and wakes to plenty. Deep rest is not surrender; it is how you will meet the spring whole.","What would it take for you to rest deeply, trusting that the world will still be there when you wake?","a woven bird’s nest holding three speckled eggs in a forked branch","the-nest"],
 ["the-gorse","The Gorse","flower","When the gorse is in flower, the old saying goes, kissing is in season, and gorse flowers nearly all year. Love is always in season for you.","Where might you let a little more love in, without waiting for the perfect moment?","a cairn of balanced stones on a windswept moorland ridge","the-cairn"],
 ["the-mayfly","The Mayfly","wheel","The mayfly dances a single day above the river and wastes none of it. Treat this one day as whole and precious; it is enough.","If today were complete in itself, with nothing owed to tomorrow, how would you spend it?","a grey heron standing on one leg in the shallows of a reed-fringed pool","the-heron"],
 ["two-cups","The Two Cups","crystal","Two cups poured from the same pot taste of the same afternoon. Love is often this plain: someone who keeps a place for you, and notices when it is empty.","Who keeps a place for you without being asked, and when did you last tell them it matters?","a glowing hearth with a teapot and a sleeping cat","the-hearth"],
 ["lit-window","The Lit Window","sun","Somewhere a window is lit because someone hoped you would come home. You are more expected, more missed and more welcome than your tired heart allows itself to believe.","Whose light have you been walking past, too sure you would be a burden at their door?","a sailing ship far out on the horizon heading toward a lit harbour","distant-ship"],
 ["mended-bowl","The Mended Bowl","crystal","A bowl mended with gold is more precious for its seam. The place where you and another broke and came back together can become the most beautiful part of the story.","Which broken bond might be worth mending, not to return to how it was, but to make something truer?","a spider’s web strung with dewdrops in early morning sunlight","the-web"],
 ["the-embrace","The Embrace","lily","Wrap your own arms around the one who has carried you this far. You have been waiting for a tenderness you are entirely able to give yourself today.","What would you say to yourself tonight if you spoke as you would to someone you dearly love?","a white swan gliding across a misty pond at dawn","the-swan"],
 ["garden-gate","The Garden Gate","key","A gate is not a refusal; it is how a garden stays a garden. Choose gently who may enter, and what you love will have room to flourish.","Where have you left your gate swinging open, and what has wandered in that you never invited?","a walled garden glimpsed through an ivy-covered gate","hidden-garden"],
 ["waiting-shore","The Waiting Shore","ship","Longing is not emptiness; it is the heart remembering its true shape. Let it ache a little, and let it point you, softly, towards what you are truly seeking.","If your longing could speak plainly, what would it say it is truly reaching for?","a pale moth with long trailing wings resting on a birch branch under the moon","the-moth"],
 ["shared-table","The Shared Table","sun","There is a seat at the table that is yours by right, not by merit. Sit down, pass the bread, and let yourself belong without having to earn it.","Where do you still behave like a guest in places where you are truly family?","a fresh loaf of bread cooling on a wooden table beside a jug of milk","daily-bread"],
 ["lamp-held-close","The Lamp Held Close","eye","Someone sees you, not the polished version but the true one, and they are staying. Let yourself be known a little more today; it is safer than you fear.","What part of yourself do you hide first when someone draws near, and why that part?","a serene open eye framed by a crescent and scattered stars","watchful-eye"],
 ["two-oars","The Two Oars","ship","Two oars, one boat, and neither rowing harder than the other. Love moves best when both of you pull gently, trusting the rhythm you are learning together.","Where in your closest bond are you rowing alone, and have you ever said so aloud?","wind filling the sails of a small boat","the-wind"],
 ["untied-knot","The Untied Knot","key","Forgiveness is not a door you hold open for another; it is a knot you untie in your own chest. Loosen it slowly; you are the one who walks free.","What resentment have you been carrying as if letting it go would mean the hurt never mattered?","a folded letter sealed with red wax beside a quill and inkwell","sealed-letter"],
 ["old-friend","The Old Friend","tree","An old friendship is a tree you do not have to plant again each spring. Its roots remember you, even after long silences, and its shade is still waiting.","Which friendship has survived your absences, and what would it mean to return to it without apology?","an ancient tree with deep roots visible beneath the earth, stars in its branches","old-tree"],
 ["borrowed-flame","The Borrowed Flame","sun","One candle lighting another loses nothing of its own flame. Give your warmth freely today; love is the only fire that grows by being shared.","Whose light have you feared would dim your own, and what if it could only brighten it?","a single candle flame glowing at dawn","first-light"],
 ["inherited-quilt","The Inherited Quilt","wheel","You are stitched from many hands: grandmothers, strangers, friends who became kin. Wrap yourself in that quilt tonight; you have never once been as alone as you feared.","Which patch of love in your life came from somewhere you never expected it?","an unfinished tapestry on an old wooden loom","the-tapestry"],
 ["honest-no","The Honest No","key","A loving no is a gift to you both. It keeps your yes clean, warm and true, and it teaches others where the real you lives.","Which yes have you given lately that was really a no wearing its kindest coat?","a golden key glowing on a velvet cushion","golden-key"],
 ["pressed-rose","The Pressed Rose","flower","Some loves are pressed between the pages of us, faded yet still fragrant. Keep what was beautiful; let the rest return to the earth with your blessing.","Which past love still teaches you something tender, now that the ache has softened?","an open music box with a tiny turning swan and a brass comb","music-box"],
 ["warm-stone","The Warm Stone","crystal","Hold yourself as a sun-warmed stone holds the afternoon: patiently, without effort. You do not have to become worthy of your own kindness; you already are.","What small comfort have you denied yourself today, waiting to feel you had deserved it?","a cairn of balanced stones on a windswept moorland ridge","the-cairn"],
 ["swallows-return","The Swallows’ Return","star","The swallows find the same eaves each spring across a thousand miles. There is a place, and there are people, your heart still knows how to fly back to.","Where does your heart fly when it needs to feel at home, and how long is it since you went?","a skein of wild geese flying in a long V over autumn fields at dusk","wild-geese"],
 ["listening-shell","The Listening Shell","eye","Hold a shell to your ear and the whole sea is there. Someone longs to hear you as fully; speak the quiet thing, and let it be received.","What have you never said aloud to the person who most needs to hear it from you?","a cross-section of a nautilus shell showing its spiralling chambers","the-nautilus"],
 ["linked-hands","The Linked Hands","path","Two hands walking side by side are not a cage but a lantern. Let yourself be accompanied today; the road is no less yours for being shared.","Where do you insist on walking alone, when someone beside you has quietly offered their hand?","a weathered wooden bench for two beneath a flowering lime tree at evening","the-bench"],
 ["lost-glove","The Lost Glove","moon","A single glove waits on the railing for the hand that lost it. What is missing from you is also missing you; love always leaves room for reunion.","Whom do you miss so quietly that even you have stopped noticing the absence?","a single trail of footprints crossing a fresh snowfield under a pale winter sky","snow-tracks"],
 ["merciful-verdict","The Merciful Verdict","lily","You have been judge and jury over one small mistake for far too long. Set down the gavel tonight; mercy is a verdict you are allowed to reach.","What would it take to forgive yourself as readily as you would forgive a dear friend?","a single feather drifting on a breeze","the-feather"],
 ["shared-silence","The Shared Silence","moon","Some love needs no words at all, only two people resting in the same quiet. Trust the silences you share; they speak a language older than speech.","With whom can you be silent and still feel completely at ease, and have you told them?","a mirror-still lake reflecting the moon","still-water"],
 ["open-palm","The Open Palm","flower","A closed fist cannot be held. Open your hand today, in welcome or in letting go, and see how gently life fills the space you have made.","What are you gripping so tightly in love that it can no longer breathe?","a dandelion clock releasing its seeds into a summer breeze","the-dandelion"],
 ["the-lullaby","The Lullaby","moon","The old lullaby still lives in your bones, sung by someone who loved you before you could understand. Hum it to the child in you tonight; they are listening.","What did love sound like when you were small, and where do you still hear it now?","a nightingale singing on a moonlit branch","nightingale"],
 ["kindred-spirit","The Kindred Spirit","star","Somewhere a kindred soul is looking for exactly your oddness, your laughter, your particular light. Be unmistakably yourself today; it is how they will recognise you.","Which part of you do you soften to fit in that might be the very thing someone is seeking?","an old wooden harp standing alone in a sunlit room","the-harp"],
 ["thawing-heart","The Thawing Heart","sun","Even the frozen river remembers how to run. Let one tender thing reach you today, and feel how readily the ice in you agrees to soften.","What hurt taught you to guard your heart, and is the guard still keeping you safe or only cold?","snowdrops pushing up through a thin layer of late snow","the-snowdrop"],
 ["small-courtesy","The Small Courtesy","flower","Love is mostly made of small courtesies: the kettle filled, the coat held, the message answered. Offer one today, and watch something quietly bloom between you.","Which ordinary kindness from someone close have you stopped noticing, and how might you thank them?","cherry blossoms drifting in spring light","the-blossom"],
 ["neighbouring-oaks","The Neighbouring Oaks","tree","Two oaks planted near each other weave their roots together beneath the ground. Close enough to shelter, far enough to grow: this is how lasting love stands.","Do you and the one you love leave each other enough room to grow towards your own light?","a great oak holding fast in a gale","deep-roots"],
 ["spoken-name","The Spoken Name","star","Somewhere today your name will be spoken with warmth by someone who is glad you exist. You are remembered fondly in rooms you will never enter.","Whose name do you say with warmth when they are not there, and do they know it?","birds singing in the trees as dawn breaks","dawn-chorus"],
 ["soft-bandage","The Soft Bandage","lily","Tend the old wound the way you would a child’s scraped knee: kneel down, look closely, and be gentle. Healing listens most of all to tenderness.","Which wound do you keep scolding for taking so long to heal, and what might it need instead?","a white lily in soft moonlight with dew on its petals","white-lily"],
 ["unmet-beloved","The Unmet Beloved","star","The one you have been hoping for is also learning, somewhere, how to love well. Keep becoming yourself; you are preparing a welcome for someone who is preparing too.","What kind of love are you ready to receive, and are you offering yourself that same love now?","a figure gazing at the heavens through a brass telescope","stargazer"],
 ["river-bank","The River Bank","ship","The river is strong because its banks hold it. Your limits do not make you less loving; they give your love a shape, a direction and a song.","Where would a clearer edge help your care flow freely instead of spilling everywhere?","a river winding through a moonlit valley","the-river"],
 ["family-tree","The Family Tree","tree","You are a new branch on an old tree, free to grow in your own direction. Honour the roots, and bloom in ways they never dared to.","Which part of your family story would you most like to rewrite in your own way of loving?","a wicker basket of rosy apples beneath a laden orchard bough","the-orchard"],
 ["moons-pull","The Moon’s Pull","moon","The moon never touches the sea, yet the tide rises to meet her every night. Distance cannot undo a true bond; love reaches further than arms ever could.","Who do you love across a distance, and how might you let them feel your pull today?","the tide rolling back over a moonlit beach","returning-tide"],
 ["self-portrait","The Self Portrait","eye","Paint yourself as love would see you: every line earned, every shadow honest, every colour your own. That portrait is truer than any you have feared.","If someone who adored you described you tonight, which of their words would surprise you most?","an ornate hand mirror reflecting a starry sky","the-mirror"],
 ["borrowed-coat","The Borrowed Coat","path","A friend’s coat around your shoulders on a cold road: this is love in plain clothes. Accept the warmth that is offered without counting what you owe.","Why does receiving care feel harder than giving it, and what would it ask of you simply to accept?","the pole star shining above a lone traveller on a path","north-star"],
 ["night-watch","The Night Watch","eye","You do not need the right words to comfort someone. Sit beside them in the dark; your presence is the lamp, and it is already enough.","Who in your life needs your company more than your answers just now, and can you offer it?","an owl perched on an ancient tree at night","the-owl"],
 ["rose-thorn","The Rose and Thorn","flower","The rose keeps her thorns and loses none of her sweetness. You may be tender and protected at once; softness was never meant to mean defenceless.","Where have you mistaken being kind for having no edges at all, and what has it cost you?","a flowering hawthorn hedgerow alive with small birds along a country lane","the-hedgerow"],
 ["the-reunion","The Reunion","path","Paths that parted long ago can curve back towards each other. Keep a light in the window of your heart; not every goodbye was the last word.","Is there someone you parted from whom you would gladly meet again, and what would you say first?","a stone bridge arching over a misty river","the-bridge"],
 ["cherished-self","The Cherished Self","crystal","You are the one companion who will walk every day of your life beside you. Make that friendship kind, and every other love will have firmer ground to stand on.","What kind of companion have you been to yourself this week, and what would you change?","a golden chalice overflowing with starlight","the-chalice"],
 ["welcome-mat","The Welcome Mat","key","Somewhere a door is already unlatched for you. Belonging is not a test you pass but a home you are allowed to walk into, muddy shoes and all.","Where are you still waiting for an invitation that, in truth, was given to you long ago?","an ancient arched door standing ajar with light beyond","open-door"],
 ["kept-confidence","The Kept Confidence","crystal","What is entrusted to you is a small, clear jewel. Hold others’ hearts carefully today, and you will find your own held with the same quiet care.","Whom do you trust with your most tender things, and what made that trust possible?","a faceted quartz crystal catching starlight and splitting it into soft colour","clear-crystal"],
 ["the-wren","The Wren","tree","The tiny wren sings louder than birds ten times her size. Your love need not be grand to be heard; offer it in your own small, bright voice.","What small way of loving comes most naturally to you, and do you honour it as real love?","a woven bird’s nest holding three speckled eggs in a forked branch","the-nest"],
 ["second-spring","The Second Spring","wheel","Love has its seasons, and winter is one of them. Do not mistake a quiet season for an ending; tended with patience, a second spring may be coming to you both.","Which bond in your life is in a winter that might simply need patience rather than a verdict?","a wheel of the four seasons, spring blossom to winter frost around its rim","turning-wheel"],
 ["clean-slate","The Clean Slate","sun","Every dawn wipes the slate clean without being asked. Offer someone, perhaps yourself, the same morning: a fresh start, freely given, with yesterday allowed to rest.","Whom might you meet tomorrow as if for the first time, letting yesterday’s quarrel stay in yesterday?","a sun just clearing the horizon, long rays fanning over a still sea","rising-sun"],
 ["the-unmasking","The Unmasking","eye","The masks were kind to you once; they kept you safe. Set one aside today with someone you trust, and let your real face feel the air.","Which mask did you learn to wear in order to be loved, and who might welcome you without it?","a solar eclipse with a glowing corona","the-eclipse"],
 ["binary-star","The Binary Star","star","Two stars can circle one another for a million years, each keeping its own fire. Lasting love lets both of you burn brightly and never asks either to dim.","Where have you dimmed yourself to keep the peace, and what would it be to shine together instead?","two moons rising side by side over the sea","two-moons"],
 ["safe-harbour","The Safe Harbour","ship","You do not have to be strong in every harbour. Let someone hold your ropes tonight while you rest; being cared for is also a way of loving.","Who is your safe harbour, and have you let them see you when the weather is rough?","an old iron anchor resting on a sandy seabed among swaying kelp","the-anchor"],
 ["unbroken-ring","The Unbroken Ring","wheel","A ring has no beginning and no end, like the vow you can make to yourself today: to stay, to listen, and never again to abandon your own heart.","What promise could you make to yourself tonight, and keep, simply because you are worth keeping faith with?","a ring of mushrooms in a mossy woodland glade by moonlight","fairy-ring"],
 ["moonlit-lane","The Moonlit Lane","moon","The moon lends her light to every lonely traveller and asks nothing in return. Be that soft light for one person today; your kindness may be their whole night’s glow.","Who is walking a lonely stretch right now, and what small light could you send their way tomorrow?","a slender crescent moon resting in a hush of dark-blue night and soft clouds","quiet-moon"],
 ["wildflower-meadow","The Wildflower Meadow","flower","No one asked the wildflower to earn its place in the meadow. You belong here as surely as poppies belong to summer; take root, and let yourself be seen.","Where have you been asking permission simply to exist, and what if you stopped asking?","a wooden rope swing hanging from a high bough over a summer meadow","the-swing"],
 ["weathered-hands","The Weathered Hands","wheel","Hands that have held each other through many winters grow beautiful in a way youth cannot imitate. Every year of faithful love adds another ring of gold.","What love in your life has grown deeper with time, and how might you honour its long years?","an antique hourglass on a wooden desk, sand falling in a thin bright stream","the-hourglass"],
 ["the-anvil","The Anvil","sun","Every strike upon the anvil is a small act of faith. What you shape with patient hands today will hold its form long after the fire has cooled.","Which piece of your work deserves another patient strike, rather than being set aside as finished too soon?","glowing embers in an old stone hearth","the-ember"],
 ["first-furrow","The First Furrow","path","The field looks vast only before the plough goes in. Cut one straight furrow today, and the whole land begins to understand what you intend.","What large undertaking might feel lighter if you asked yourself only for the first honest furrow?","a seedling sprouting from dark rich soil","the-seed"],
 ["potters-wheel","The Potter’s Wheel","wheel","The clay collapses many times before it learns its shape. Each wobble on the wheel is your hands remembering; keep your centre, and the vessel will rise.","Where have you mistaken the ordinary collapse of learning for proof that you are not meant to do this?","an unfinished tapestry on an old wooden loom","the-tapestry"],
 ["unwritten-page","The Unwritten Page","key","The blank page is not empty; it is listening. Set down one true sentence, and the rest of your story will find the courage to follow.","What would you write today if you knew no one would ever read it but you?","a folded letter sealed with red wax beside a quill and inkwell","sealed-letter"],
 ["raised-sail","The Raised Sail","ship","A ship in harbour is safe, yet that was never what she was built for. Raise one sail today; the open water has been expecting you.","Which safety in your life has quietly become a harbour you are now afraid to leave?","wind filling the sails of a small boat","the-wind"],
 ["iron-gate","The Iron Gate","key","The gate is heavier than it looks and lighter than you fear. Lean your whole weight against it once, and the hinges will remember how to sing.","What door have you been pushing with only half your strength, keeping the rest in reserve for retreat?","an ancient arched door standing ajar with light beyond","open-door"],
 ["climbing-rose","The Climbing Rose","flower","The rose climbs the old wall one tendril at a time, never asking whether it is allowed. Reach towards your light today; the stone will hold you.","What would you reach for if you trusted that the walls around you could become your support?","a walled garden glimpsed through an ivy-covered gate","hidden-garden"],
 ["the-whetstone","The Whetstone","crystal","The blade is not made sharp in a day, but by faithful strokes upon the stone. Return to your practice; each patient pass brings a finer edge.","Which skill would grow keener if you came back to it a little every day, without hurry?","a cairn of balanced stones on a windswept moorland ridge","the-cairn"],
 ["sculptors-chisel","The Sculptor’s Chisel","crystal","The figure already lives inside the stone. Each careful cut takes away only what was never you, and slowly your true shape steps into the light.","What could you chip away from your days so that what matters most has room to show itself?","a faceted quartz crystal catching starlight and splitting it into soft colour","clear-crystal"],
 ["final-stitch","The Final Stitch","wheel","The last stitch is the one that holds all the others. Return to what you began with tender hands; finishing is its own kind of magic.","What unfinished thing still tugs at your sleeve, and what would it truly ask of you to complete it?","a loom weaving golden threads into a tapestry of stars","the-weaver"],
 ["heralds-horn","The Herald’s Horn","star","There is a note in you that only you can sound. Raise your voice today, gently or boldly, and let the world hear what has waited so long.","What have you been leaving unsaid because you feared your voice would not be welcome?","a bronze bell hanging in an open stone belfry beneath the stars","the-bell"],
 ["the-tightrope","The Tightrope","star","Every crossing high above the ground is made of a thousand tiny corrections. Keep your eyes on the far post; your balance is wiser than your fear.","Where are you staring down at the drop, when you could fix your gaze on where you are going?","a pair of brass balance scales holding a rose petal and a pebble","the-scales"],
 ["alchemists-flask","The Alchemist’s Flask","crystal","Nothing in your life is wasted on the alchemist within you. Every failure, every false start, is quietly being turned to gold in the slow fire of your patience.","Which disappointment might you hold up to the light again, to see what gold it has become?","a golden chalice overflowing with starlight","the-chalice"],
 ["the-keystone","The Keystone","key","One stone at the crown of the arch holds all the others in place. Your small, steady part matters more than you know; without it, the bridge would fall.","Where is your quiet contribution holding more weight than anyone, including you, has noticed?","a stone bridge arching over a misty river","the-bridge"],
 ["new-crescent","The New Crescent","moon","The thinnest crescent is already a promise of the full moon. Begin small and begin tonight; the light will gather itself around your intention.","What intention would you set beneath tonight’s sky if you trusted it to grow a little with each passing night?","a slender crescent moon resting in a hush of dark-blue night and soft clouds","quiet-moon"],
 ["forked-wood","The Fork in the Wood","path","Two paths fade into the trees, and neither promises its ending. Choose the one that asks more of your heart, and you will never walk it alone.","If fear were not choosing for you, which of your possible roads would you be walking already?","a weathered signpost where three country roads meet","crossroads"],
 ["plumb-line","The Plumb Line","crystal","The builder trusts the plumb line over the eye. Let one true principle guide your work today, and everything you raise will stand straight and sure.","What principle keeps your life upright, and where have you been building slightly out of true?","an antique hourglass on a wooden desk, sand falling in a thin bright stream","the-hourglass"],
 ["the-ladder","The Ladder","star","No one climbs to the stars in a single leap. Rung by rung, faithful and unhurried, you are rising further than the doubting part of you can see.","Which rung are you standing on now, and can you honour it rather than resent how far is left?","a spiral staircase climbing towards the stars","the-spiral"],
 ["the-spindle","The Spindle","wheel","The spindle turns the same way every day, and from that faithful turning comes the thread for a whole cloak. Your discipline is spinning your future.","What one small repetition, kept faithfully, could become a thread strong enough to carry your dream?","an unfinished tapestry on an old wooden loom","the-tapestry"],
 ["struck-match","The Struck Match","sun","One strike, one breath of courage, and the dark room changes. You do not need a great fire to begin; only the willingness to strike.","What would you dare to light today if you stopped waiting for perfect conditions?","a single candle flame glowing at dawn","first-light"],
 ["the-falcon","The Falcon","eye","The falcon returns to the glove by choice and leaves it by courage. Fly out towards your ambition today; your sight is keener than you believe.","What ambition have you been circling for so long that it is time to descend and claim it?","a kingfisher perched on a reed above a clear brook","the-kingfisher"],
 ["unmoored-boat","The Unmoored Boat","ship","The rope slips from the post and the little boat drifts out, trembling. Let it; the current of change is carrying you towards a wider shore.","What would loosen in you if you stopped gripping the rope that ties you to the old shore?","a four-pointed guiding star above a small boat on calm water","steady-star"],
 ["shed-skin","The Shed Skin","wheel","The serpent leaves its old skin in the grass and does not mourn it. What no longer fits you was once a faithful garment; thank it, and move on.","Which old version of yourself are you still wearing out of loyalty rather than because it fits?","a cross-section of a nautilus shell showing its spiralling chambers","the-nautilus"],
 ["storm-crossing","The Storm Crossing","ship","Brave sailors are not those who never feel the swell, but those who hold the wheel through it. You are steadier on these waters than you think.","What storm have you already crossed that proves you are stronger than the one you now fear?","a lighthouse beam sweeping over a stormy sea","lighthouse"],
 ["the-apprentice","The Apprentice","key","Every master was once an apprentice who refused to stop. Be a beginner without shame today; humility is the doorway every great craft walks through.","Where might you grow faster if you allowed yourself to be seen not knowing yet?","a golden key glowing on a velvet cushion","golden-key"],
 ["pruning-knife","The Pruning Knife","tree","The wise gardener cuts back a branch so the tree can bear. Letting go of a good thing may be how you make room for the great one.","Which good but draining commitment might you prune, so that your truest work can finally bear fruit?","a wicker basket of rosy apples beneath a laden orchard bough","the-orchard"],
 ["the-mapmaker","The Mapmaker","star","No map exists for the life you are making, so you are drawing it as you go. Every brave step marks a coastline someone else will one day follow.","What territory in your life is still unmapped, and what would it take to step into it with curiosity?","a brass compass resting on an old map","the-compass"],
 ["the-banner","The Banner","sun","Unfurl what you stand for and let it catch the wind. The right people will see your colours from afar and come walking towards you.","If your values were stitched upon a banner, which ones would you be proud to fly today?","a sunset bathing rolling hills in gold","golden-hour"],
 ["the-sunflower","The Sunflower","flower","The sunflower turns its whole face towards the light, morning after morning. Turn towards what gives you life today, and you will grow tall without strain.","What gives you light, and how often do you let yourself turn your face towards it?","a single flower opening in an autumn garden while other stems rest","late-bloom"],
 ["loosed-arrow","The Loosed Arrow","eye","The arrow flies only when the archer lets go. You have drawn the bow long enough; release your aim, and trust the string you have trained.","What have you prepared for so thoroughly that the only thing left is to let it fly?","a fox watching quietly from tall grass at dusk","the-fox"],
 ["the-pearl","The Pearl","lily","The pearl begins as a grain of grit the oyster could not cast out. Your patient tending of a difficulty is quietly making something luminous.","What irritation in your life might you be slowly turning into something of quiet and lasting worth?","a great whale gliding through deep blue water beneath shafts of light","the-whale"],
 ["quiet-vow","The Quiet Vow","lily","Some vows are made by candlelight, with no witness but your own heart. Speak yours softly tonight; the quietest promise can steer the bravest life.","What would you vow to yourself tonight, knowing no one else would ever need to hear it?","a candlelit stone chapel with open arched windows","sanctuary"],
 ["floating-lantern","The Floating Lantern","lily","Set your intention on the water and let it go. Like a lantern carried downstream, it will light places you could never have reached by holding on.","What part of your plan are you ready to entrust to the current, instead of steering every ripple?","a silver thread linking two distant lanterns across the night","silver-thread"],
 ["the-ferryman","The Ferryman","ship","The ferryman knows the river by feel, not by sight. Trust the craft you have learned in the dark hours; your hands will carry you across.","What do you know in your hands and bones that your anxious mind keeps forgetting?","a sailing ship far out on the horizon heading toward a lit harbour","distant-ship"],
 ["mill-wheel","The Mill Wheel","wheel","The mill wheel turns because the water keeps arriving. Let your steady efforts flow each day, and the slow grinding will turn your grain into bread.","What daily effort feels small to you but keeps the whole wheel of your life turning?","a tall waterfall pouring into a fern-lined pool","the-waterfall"],
 ["far-horizon","The Far Horizon","eye","Lift your eyes past today’s small worries to the horizon you long for. What you can see clearly, you can begin to walk towards.","If you could see your life ten years from now, which step taken today would you thank yourself for?","a sun just clearing the horizon, long rays fanning over a still sea","rising-sun"],
 ["the-oar","The Oar","ship","Each pull of the oar seems to change nothing, and yet the shore draws nearer. Keep rowing with a steady heart; the distance is shrinking.","Where are you making real progress that you simply cannot yet see from where you sit?","the tide rolling back over a moonlit beach","returning-tide"],
 ["the-locksmith","The Locksmith","key","No lock was ever made without a key in mind. Study the problem before you patiently, and its secret will turn beneath your careful fingers.","Which problem in your life might yield if you met it with curiosity rather than force?","an ornate antique key held in open cupped hands, glowing softly","inner-key"],
 ["lions-heart","The Lion’s Heart","sun","Courage is not a roar; it is the steady heartbeat that keeps you walking forward while you tremble. That heart beats in you, golden and unafraid.","When did you last act bravely while frightened, and what did it teach you about yourself?","a stag with branching antlers standing in a misty forest clearing","the-stag"],
 ["the-sower","The Sower","tree","The sower scatters seed in faith, never knowing which will rise. Cast your efforts generously today; the harvest is not yours to count yet.","What would you offer more freely if you let go of needing to know the outcome?","golden wheat sheaves under a harvest moon","quiet-harvest"],
 ["tuning-fork","The Tuning Fork","crystal","Strike the tuning fork and it rings true, whatever the noise around it. Find the note that is yours, and let your life tune itself to it.","When do you feel most in tune with yourself, and how could you return there more often?","an old wooden harp standing alone in a sunlit room","the-harp"],
 ["the-leap","The Leap","path","There comes a moment when thinking must give way to leaping. The ground on the other side is firmer than it looks from here; gather yourself and go.","What leap have you measured so many times that measuring has become a way of never jumping?","a hare leaping over a frosted hillside beneath a full moon","the-hare"],
 ["silver-road","The Silver Road","moon","The moon lays a silver road across the water, straight to your feet. It is an invitation, not a command; you may walk it whenever you are ready.","What invitation have you received lately that you keep admiring from the safety of the shore?","a mirror-still lake reflecting the moon","still-water"],
 ["the-pilgrim","The Pilgrim","path","The pilgrim does not need to be holy; only to keep walking. Every mile you travel with an open heart is already holy ground.","What is the quiet purpose beneath your daily walking, and when did you last remember it?","the pole star shining above a lone traveller on a path","north-star"],
 ["signet-ring","The Signet Ring","key","Press your seal into the warm wax and own what you have made. Your name belongs on your work; there is nothing vain in claiming it.","Which of your achievements have you been reluctant to sign your name to, and why?","a folded letter sealed with red wax beside a quill and inkwell","sealed-letter"],
 ["desert-bloom","The Desert Bloom","flower","In the driest place, after the longest wait, the desert flowers all at once. Your persistence is storing water for a blossoming you will scarcely believe.","What has your long patience been quietly preparing in you for the moment the rain comes?","snowdrops pushing up through a thin layer of late snow","the-snowdrop"],
 ["grafted-branch","The Grafted Branch","tree","A new branch, bound with care to an old tree, soon bears its own fruit. You can join something new to all you have been, and both will flourish.","What new direction could you graft onto your life without cutting away the roots that made you?","a weeping willow trailing its long branches into a quiet stream","the-willow"],
 ["passed-torch","The Passed Torch","sun","The flame you carry was handed to you by someone who believed. Run your stretch of the road with joy, and pass it on brighter than you found it.","Whose belief in you once lit your way, and whom might you now light in turn?","a lantern held aloft in a dark forest","the-lantern"],
 ["the-weathervane","The Weathervane","wheel","The weathervane turns with every wind yet never leaves its roof. You can change direction a hundred times and still be standing on your own ground.","Which change of course have you judged as fickleness, when it may really have been wisdom?","a wheel of the four seasons, spring blossom to winter frost around its rim","turning-wheel"],
 ["eagles-eye","The Eagle’s Eye","eye","From high above, the eagle sees the whole valley and the one thing that matters within it. Rise a little today, and your purpose will come into focus.","Seen from far above your life, what would stand out as the one thing truly worth your strength?","a serene open eye framed by a crescent and scattered stars","watchful-eye"],
 ["unmade-bed","The Unmade Bed","moon","The bed you left this morning still holds the shape of your sleep. Return to it without apology tonight; rest is not a reward you earn but a tide you are owed.","What would your evenings look like if you went to bed as kindly as you would tuck in someone you love?","a slender crescent moon resting in a hush of dark-blue night and soft clouds","quiet-moon"],
 ["closing-gate","The Closing Gate","key","Some gates close so that a garden can rest. Lay your hand on the latch without bitterness; what ended here did its work, and the ground behind it is quietly healing.","Which ending in your life are you still guarding, and what might grow if you let the gate stay closed?","a walled garden glimpsed through an ivy-covered gate","hidden-garden"],
 ["last-leaf","The Last Leaf","tree","The tree does not grieve the leaf it lets go; it trusts the spring it cannot yet see. Release what has finished, and feel how much lighter your branches become.","What has already finished in your life that you are still holding on to out of loyalty?","a wheel of the four seasons, spring blossom to winter frost around its rim","turning-wheel"],
 ["low-tide","The Low Tide","ship","At low tide the shore reveals its quiet treasures: shells, pools, small bright lives. When your strength ebbs, look closely; there is beauty here that the full sea hides.","What has your tiredness shown you that you would never have noticed at full strength?","the tide rolling back over a moonlit beach","returning-tide"],
 ["sleeping-cat","The Sleeping Cat","sun","The cat sleeps in the sunlit patch without a single doubt that she deserves to. Learn from her today: find your own warm square of light and simply be.","When did you last rest without first explaining to yourself why you were allowed to?","a glowing hearth with a teapot and a sleeping cat","the-hearth"],
 ["folded-wings","The Folded Wings","lily","Even the swiftest bird folds its wings at dusk. You need not prove your flight tonight; tuck your head beneath the soft dark, and let the sky keep watch.","What are you still trying to prove at the end of the day, and to whom are you proving it?","a nightingale singing on a moonlit branch","nightingale"],
 ["lavender-sprig","The Lavender Sprig","flower","A sprig of lavender beneath the pillow, an old remedy for an old ache. Let small, fragrant comforts tend you tonight; tenderness is a medicine too, and you are worthy of it.","Which small comfort have you denied yourself because it seemed too simple to matter?","soft rain falling on a blossoming garden","gentle-rain"],
 ["unlit-candle","The Unlit Candle","sun","A candle need not burn every hour to be a light. Let yourself be unlit for a while; the flame will come again, steadier, when you are rested.","What would it mean to let yourself be unused, unlit and unproductive, just for one evening?","a single candle flame glowing at dawn","first-light"],
 ["heavy-cloak","The Heavy Cloak","key","You have worn this heavy cloak through many winters, and it kept you safe. The weather has changed; you may unfasten it now and feel the gentler air.","Which old protection served you well once, but now only weighs you down?","an ancient arched door standing ajar with light beyond","open-door"],
 ["slow-bend","The Slow Bend","path","Where the river slows at its bend, the water clears and the heron fishes. Slowing is not stopping; it is how the current finally learns to see.","What becomes clear to you only when you stop hurrying, and how could you allow more of that?","a river winding through a moonlit valley","the-river"],
 ["rosemary-bush","The Rosemary Bush","flower","Rosemary is for remembrance, and it grows best in poor soil. Your grief is a garden of love; let it flower in its own season, without hurry or shame.","Whom do you still carry with you, and how might you honour them gently today?","a walled garden glimpsed through an ivy-covered gate","hidden-garden"],
 ["empty-chair","The Empty Chair","moon","The empty chair is not only absence; it is the shape of a love that remains. Sit beside it tonight and speak softly. Nothing true between you has been lost.","What would you say tonight to someone you miss, if you trusted that love still listens?","a weathered wooden bench for two beneath a flowering lime tree at evening","the-bench"],
 ["the-balm","The Balm","crystal","Old wounds close from the inside out, slowly, with no one watching. Be patient with your mending; the deepest healing happens where only you can feel it.","Which part of you is still healing, and how might you be more patient with its pace?","a moss-covered stone well with a wooden bucket hanging from its rope","the-well"],
 ["dimmed-lamp","The Dimmed Lamp","star","Turn the lamp down low and let the evening soften its edges. You do not need to see everything tonight; some answers arrive only in half-light.","Which question have you been interrogating that might reveal itself more gently in the dark?","a lantern held aloft in a dark forest","the-lantern"],
 ["steeping-tea","The Steeping Tea","wheel","The tea will not be hurried; its colour deepens in its own good time. Let this day steep slowly, and you will taste far more of it than you expected.","What would you savour today if you gave it a few more patient minutes?","a glowing hearth with a teapot and a sleeping cat","the-hearth"],
 ["moon-bath","The Moon Bath","moon","Stand in moonlight and let it rinse the day from you. Nothing you did or failed to do clings to you here; you are washed clean and gently held.","What from today would you like to rinse away before sleep, and what would you like to keep?","a mirror-still lake reflecting the moon","still-water"],
 ["full-cup","The Full Cup","crystal","Your cup is full already, though the world keeps urging you to pour more in. Stop and taste what is there; enough has been quietly waiting for you all along.","Where in your life is it already enough, if only you allowed yourself to call it so?","a golden chalice overflowing with starlight","the-chalice"],
 ["sleeping-bear","The Sleeping Bear","tree","The bear goes into the hill and sleeps the whole winter without guilt. Retreat is part of your wildness too; you will wake when the world is warm again.","What season of retreat are you being asked to honour, rather than push your way through?","an ancient tree with deep roots visible beneath the earth, stars in its branches","old-tree"],
 ["washing-line","The Washing Line","sun","Hang your worries on the line and let the wind and sun take their turn. Some things only come clean when you stop scrubbing and leave them to the air.","Which worry might soften if you stopped working at it and simply let time air it out?","a diamond-shaped kite with a ribboned tail flying high above a windy meadow","the-kite"],
 ["uncurled-hand","The Uncurled Hand","lily","Uncurl your fingers, one by one. The things you have clutched so long were never meant to be held this tightly. An open palm receives as gracefully as it releases.","What are you gripping so hard that your hands have forgotten how to receive?","an ornate antique key held in open cupped hands, glowing softly","inner-key"],
 ["vesper-hour","The Vesper Hour","star","At vespers the old houses lit a single candle and let the day be done. Mark your own ending tonight; a day well closed is a gift to tomorrow.","How do you close your days, and what small ritual might help you lay them down?","a candlelit stone chapel with open arched windows","sanctuary"],
 ["healing-spring","The Healing Spring","crystal","Deep in the hillside a warm spring rises, as it has for a thousand years. There is a source of renewal in you that no exhaustion has ever reached.","What has always restored you, and when did you last allow yourself to return to it?","a tall waterfall pouring into a fern-lined pool","the-waterfall"],
 ["white-hush","The White Hush","crystal","Snow falls, and the whole world lowers its voice. Let this hush settle over you; beneath the white, everything is resting, and so, at last, may you.","What noise in your life could you quieten, even for an hour, to let yourself truly rest?","a single trail of footprints crossing a fresh snowfield under a pale winter sky","snow-tracks"],
 ["passing-storm","The Passing Storm","flower","The storm has passed and the garden is dripping, bruised and alive. Recovery is not returning to who you were; it is tenderly meeting who you have become.","Who have you become since your hardest season, and can you greet that person with kindness?","soft rain falling on a blossoming garden","gentle-rain"],
 ["long-exhale","The Long Exhale","lily","You have been holding your breath for longer than you know. Let it go now, slowly, all the way down; the body remembers peace the moment you allow it.","What would your body tell you, if you listened to it as closely as you listen to your thoughts?","a single feather drifting on a breeze","the-feather"],
 ["beached-boat","The Beached Boat","ship","The little boat is drawn up on the shingle for mending. There is no shame in being out of the water; this is how a vessel lasts for many voyages.","What would it mean to pause for repair before the next voyage, rather than waiting until you are sinking?","wind filling the sails of a small boat","the-wind"],
 ["closing-daisy","The Closing Daisy","flower","The daisy folds her petals every evening and opens them again at dawn. Closing is not defeat; it is how the brightest things keep their light.","When you close yourself off to rest, do you treat it as a retreat or as a renewal?","a weathered stone sundial in a summer garden, its shadow falling across its face","the-sundial"],
 ["lowered-sail","The Lowered Sail","ship","Lower the sail, and let the boat rock gently at its mooring. The wind will still be here tomorrow; tonight the harbour asks nothing of you at all.","Which ambition could you lay down tonight, trusting it will still be there in the morning?","a sailing ship far out on the horizon heading toward a lit harbour","distant-ship"],
 ["patchwork-quilt","The Patchwork Quilt","wheel","Your life is a patchwork of worn and lovely pieces, stitched by hands that cared. Wrap yourself in it tonight; every square has kept somebody warm.","Which piece of your past, once ragged, now forms part of what comforts you?","an unfinished tapestry on an old wooden loom","the-tapestry"],
 ["rest-note","The Rest Note","wheel","In music the rest is written as carefully as any note. Your silence belongs to the song; without it, nothing you play would have any shape at all.","Where might a deliberate pause give shape to a day that has been all sound?","an old wooden harp standing alone in a sunlit room","the-harp"],
 ["kind-nurse","The Kind Nurse","eye","Speak to yourself today as a nurse speaks to a feverish child: softly, without blame. You are doing far better than the harsh voice within you will admit.","What would your inner voice sound like if it had only ever been kind to you?","a white lily in soft moonlight with dew on its petals","white-lily"],
 ["bare-branches","The Bare Branches","tree","In winter the bare branches let the sky shine through them. Stripped of what you thought you needed, you may find there is more light in you than ever.","What did losing something dear show you about what you truly need to feel whole?","an ancient tree with deep roots visible beneath the earth, stars in its branches","old-tree"],
 ["the-nightlight","The Nightlight","moon","A small light left on in the hall has comforted many a frightened child. Leave one on for yourself tonight; there is no age at which we stop needing to feel safe.","What helps you feel safe at night, and have you allowed yourself enough of it lately?","a silver thread linking two distant lanterns across the night","silver-thread"],
 ["banked-fire","The Banked Fire","sun","Bank the fire at night and it will glow until morning. You need not blaze every hour; covered and quiet, your warmth is keeping itself alive.","How might you conserve your warmth for what matters, instead of burning bright for everything?","glowing embers in an old stone hearth","the-ember"],
 ["the-hammock","The Hammock","tree","Strung between two trees, the hammock asks only that you lie back and trust it. You have carried yourself so far; let something else hold your weight today.","Who or what could you trust to hold you today, so that you need not hold yourself?","a wooden rope swing hanging from a high bough over a summer meadow","the-swing"],
 ["salt-tears","The Salt Tears","crystal","Tears carry salt from the same sea that cradled the first life. Let them fall without apology; they are cleansing a place in you that is ready to heal.","When did you last let yourself cry fully, and what did you feel in the quiet afterwards?","a great whale gliding through deep blue water beneath shafts of light","the-whale"],
 ["fishermans-net","The Fisherman’s Net","ship","The fisherman sits on the quay mending his nets between tides. Your quiet repairs are not idle hours; they are what makes the next catch possible.","What in your life needs gentle mending before you feel ready to set out again?","an old iron anchor resting on a sandy seabed among swaying kelp","the-anchor"],
 ["casement-window","The Casement Window","eye","Open the window and let the old air out. Stale thoughts leave quietly when they are given a way, and the evening breeze brings something clean and new.","Which stale thought has been circulating in you, and what would let some fresh air in?","delicate frost ferns spreading across a cottage window pane","the-frost"],
 ["wayside-inn","The Wayside Inn","path","Every pilgrim needs a wayside inn: a fire, a bed and no questions asked. You have walked far; stop here tonight, and the road will wait for you.","Where have you been refusing to stop, as though rest were a detour from the journey?","the pole star shining above a lone traveller on a path","north-star"],
 ["settling-sand","The Settling Sand","eye","Shake the jar and all is clouded; set it down and the sand settles of its own accord. Your mind will clear too, if you will only stop stirring it.","What are you stirring again and again that might settle if you simply set it down?","an antique hourglass on a wooden desk, sand falling in a thin bright stream","the-hourglass"],
 ["closed-book","The Closed Book","key","Close the book on this chapter with gratitude, not haste. You may take it down and read it again one day, but tonight the story asks you to rest.","Which chapter of your life is ready to be closed, and what would you thank it for?","a folded letter sealed with red wax beside a quill and inkwell","sealed-letter"],
 ["wildflower-verge","The Wildflower Verge","flower","Nobody tends the wildflowers on the verge, and still they bloom. You need not be perfect, or perfectly cared for, to flourish; you are already enough as you are.","In what ways are you already flourishing, without the perfect conditions you once believed you needed?","a dandelion clock releasing its seeds into a summer breeze","the-dandelion"],
 ["slow-dawn","The Slow Dawn","star","Not every dawn arrives in a blaze. Some come grey and gradual, the light seeping in so slowly you cannot name the moment. So, too, does healing arrive.","Which small sign tells you that you are, slowly, feeling better than you were?","a sun just clearing the horizon, long rays fanning over a still sea","rising-sun"],
 ["dream-keeper","The Dream Keeper","moon","Tonight your dreams will carry a message folded small. Keep a pen beside your bed; what the night whispers, the morning is meant to remember and gently unfold.","Which dream, sleeping or waking, keeps returning to you, and what might it want you to notice at last?","a slender crescent moon resting in a hush of dark-blue night and soft clouds","quiet-moon"],
 ["falling-star","The Falling Star","star","A star let go of the sky so that someone below might make a wish. Your letting go is never wasted; somewhere, it quietly becomes another’s hope.","What have you released this year that may have made room for someone else’s good fortune?","a comet with a long luminous tail streaking above a sleeping village","the-comet"],
 ["second-sight","The Second Sight","eye","You notice more than you admit. That flicker of knowing before the words arrive is not imagination; it is your soul reading the room. Trust it today.","When did your first instinct about someone turn out to be right, and did you honour it at the time?","a serene open eye framed by a crescent and scattered stars","watchful-eye"],
 ["night-garden","The Night Garden","flower","Some flowers open only after dark, pouring out their scent for no audience but the stars. Your quiet gifts are no less fragrant for being unseen.","What do you offer the world in your private hours that deserves your own gratitude tonight?","a white lily in soft moonlight with dew on its petals","white-lily"],
 ["star-chart","The Star Chart","star","Long ago someone drew lines between the stars and saw a story. Join the scattered moments of your life today; a shape is emerging, and it is beautiful.","If you joined the brightest moments of this past year, what picture of yourself would appear?","a figure gazing at the heavens through a brass telescope","stargazer"],
 ["thankful-glass","The Thankful Glass","crystal","Gratitude is a lens of clear glass. Hold it up to the plainest morning, and the hidden gold in every small and faithful thing will begin to shine.","Name three ordinary things from today that you would miss terribly if they were suddenly gone.","a faceted quartz crystal catching starlight and splitting it into soft colour","clear-crystal"],
 ["twin-clocks","The Twin Clocks","wheel","You glance up and the hour repeats itself, or a stranger speaks the very words in your head. Coincidence is the universe clearing its throat; lean closer and listen.","What small coincidence lately felt like a nod, and what were you thinking about when it came?","an antique hourglass on a wooden desk, sand falling in a thin bright stream","the-hourglass"],
 ["paper-boat","The Paper Boat","ship","Fold a paper boat and set it on the stream. Not everything must be useful to be holy; a little play is how the soul remembers it is free.","What playful thing did you once do without thinking, and what stops you from doing it this week?","a river winding through a moonlit valley","the-river"],
 ["sleeping-sea","The Sleeping Sea","ship","In sleep you sail to shores the waking mind cannot reach. Do not dismiss what you bring back; even fragments are precious cargo from a deeper country.","If your dreams were letters from a wiser part of you, what has the latest one been trying to say?","a sailing ship far out on the horizon heading toward a lit harbour","distant-ship"],
 ["milky-way","The Milky Way","star","You are made of the same old light that spills across the night sky. When you feel small, remember that the universe went to great lengths to make you.","What would you treat more gently today if you truly believed you were made of starlight?","curtains of the northern lights rippling over a snowy pine forest","the-aurora"],
 ["lucky-penny","The Lucky Penny","key","A coin face up on the pavement, a song at exactly the right moment: small graces are scattered along your way. Pick them up; they are proof you are noticed.","Which small stroke of luck this month have you hurried past without stopping to give thanks?","a golden key glowing on a velvet cushion","golden-key"],
 ["tide-clock","The Tide Clock","wheel","The sea keeps time by the Moon, not by the clock. Your life has its own tides too; honour the pull of rest as faithfully as the pull of effort.","Where in your week are you living by the clock’s time when your body is asking for the tide’s?","the tide rolling back over a moonlit beach","returning-tide"],
 ["spinning-top","The Spinning Top","wheel","Watch a spinning top: it stays upright only while it dances. Perhaps your balance today lies not in holding perfectly still, but in a little joyful movement.","What lightness could you bring to a task that has grown heavy with too much seriousness?","an open music box with a tiny turning swan and a brass comb","music-box"],
 ["window-candle","The Window Candle","sun","Somewhere a candle has been left burning in a window for you. You are expected; whatever road you are on, there is a place that longs for your arrival.","Where do you feel most expected and welcomed, and when did you last let yourself go there?","a single candle flame glowing at dawn","first-light"],
 ["cradle-moon","The Cradle Moon","moon","The young crescent lies on her back like a cradle, holding the whole dark sky. Something tender is newly born in you; rock it gently before you ask it to walk.","What new hope in you needs nurture and patience now, rather than quick results?","a slender crescent moon resting in a hush of dark-blue night and soft clouds","quiet-moon"],
 ["hazel-wand","The Hazel Wand","tree","The diviner walks the fields with a hazel twig and trusts the tremble in her hands. You carry a quiet instrument too; when it trembles, there is water near.","What does your body do when something is right for you, and how often do you pause to notice it?","a flowering hawthorn hedgerow alive with small birds along a country lane","the-hedgerow"],
 ["tea-leaves","The Tea Leaves","eye","The leaves settle at the bottom of the cup in shapes only you can read. Meaning is not pressed upon you from outside; it rises from what you are ready to see.","What pattern have you glimpsed in your life lately that others might miss, and what does it mean to you?","a glowing hearth with a teapot and a sleeping cat","the-hearth"],
 ["wandering-planets","The Wandering Planets","star","The planets were once called wanderers, yet they keep perfect time. Your wandering is not lost; it follows an orbit too wide to see from where you stand.","Where has some seemingly aimless wandering led you somewhere that now feels as though it was meant to be?","a four-pointed guiding star above a small boat on calm water","steady-star"],
 ["snow-globe","The Snow Globe","crystal","Shake the globe and the little world goes white and wild; wait, and it settles into clarity. Give your swirling thoughts a moment, and they will fall into place.","What decision might become clear if you allowed the snow to settle for one more day?","delicate frost ferns spreading across a cottage window pane","the-frost"],
 ["the-daydream","The Daydream","lily","Let your mind drift out of the window for a while. Daydreams are not idleness; they are the soul’s quiet scouts, mapping lands you will one day walk.","Where does your mind wander when no one is asking anything of you, and what is it looking for?","a single feather drifting on a breeze","the-feather"],
 ["tree-rings","The Tree Rings","tree","Each year leaves a ring inside the tree, the lean ones and the generous alike. You carry every season you have lived through, and together they make you whole.","Which lean year of your life laid down a ring of strength that you can still feel today?","an ancient tree with deep roots visible beneath the earth, stars in its branches","old-tree"],
 ["the-fireflies","The Fireflies","sun","Fireflies flicker into the dusk as if the meadow were dreaming of stars. Small joys arrive the same way: unannounced, brief and luminous. Be out in the evening to catch them.","What tiny, fleeting delight lit up your day, and how might you make more room for such moments?","a sunset bathing rolling hills in gold","golden-hour"],
 ["the-riddle","The Riddle","key","Not every question is meant to be answered at once. Carry the riddle gently in your pocket; one ordinary afternoon it will turn over and show you its key.","Which unanswered question could you live alongside a little longer, rather than forcing it to resolve?","an ornate antique key held in open cupped hands, glowing softly","inner-key"],
 ["sky-lantern","The Sky Lantern","sun","Write your thanks upon a paper lantern and let it rise. What leaves your hands in gratitude does not vanish; it becomes a small light for the whole night sky.","Whom would you thank tonight if you knew your words would reach them, wherever they now are?","a silver thread linking two distant lanterns across the night","silver-thread"],
 ["blue-hour","The Blue Hour","moon","Between sunset and darkness there is a blue hour when the world holds its breath. You may be in such an hour now; it is not an ending, but a hush before wonder.","What in-between time in your life might be asking you to pause, rather than hurry on to the next thing?","a worn wooden stile set in a dry-stone wall between two misty fields","the-stile"],
 ["the-geode","The Geode","crystal","A plain grey stone, cracked open, reveals a cave of amethyst. The plainest-seeming day may hold a hidden chamber of wonder; be willing to look within.","Which part of yourself have you judged as ordinary that might hold something remarkable inside?","a pomegranate split open to reveal its jewelled seeds on a pewter plate","the-pomegranate"],
 ["third-eye","The Third Eye","eye","Between your brows sits a quiet window that opens inward. Close your outer eyes for a few breaths today; what you see behind them is every bit as true.","What image or feeling appears when you close your eyes and simply ask what you truly need?","an owl perched on an ancient tree at night","the-owl"],
 ["cloud-shapes","The Cloud Shapes","path","Lie back and let the clouds become dragons, ships and faces. The imagination that sees them is the very same one that will dream your next chapter into being.","When did you last lie still long enough to find a shape in the clouds, and what might you see today?","a striped hot-air balloon drifting over a patchwork of fields","the-balloon"],
 ["the-pendulum","The Pendulum","wheel","The pendulum swings and swings, and still it marks the true hour. Your back and forth is not mere indecision; it is your heart finding its honest centre.","Which choice have you been swinging over, and what does the stillness at its centre tell you?","a pair of brass balance scales holding a rose petal and a pebble","the-scales"],
 ["pilgrim-shell","The Pilgrim’s Shell","path","A scallop shell marks the pilgrim’s road. You may never have named it, but you are on a sacred journey, and every ordinary step today counts as part of it.","If your everyday life were a pilgrimage, what would you be walking towards?","a cairn of balanced stones on a windswept moorland ridge","the-cairn"],
 ["night-voyage","The Night Voyage","ship","You set out not knowing what lies beyond the dark water, and still the stars keep you company. Faith is simply sailing on while the shore is out of sight.","What journey are you making without seeing its destination, and what keeps you company along the way?","a lighthouse beam sweeping over a stormy sea","lighthouse"],
 ["wind-chime","The Wind Chime","lily","Every breeze passes, yet the chime remembers how to sing. Let today’s small moments move through you, and notice the music they make on their way.","What sound, voice or song brought you an unexpected moment of peace today?","a bronze bell hanging in an open stone belfry beneath the stars","the-bell"],
 ["laughing-brook","The Laughing Brook","path","The brook laughs all the way down the hill, over every stone in its path. You too can meet the obstacles of the day with a little music rather than a frown.","What obstacle might feel lighter today if you met it with humour instead of strain?","flat stepping stones crossing a shallow, rushing stream","stepping-stones"],
 ["old-soul","The Old Soul","tree","You were born remembering things you were never taught. That ancient tenderness in you is no accident; it has walked a long way to be here, in you, now.","What wisdom do you carry that seems older than your years, and where do you sense it came from?","a great oak holding fast in a gale","deep-roots"],
 ["the-moonstone","The Moonstone","crystal","The moonstone holds a soft light that shifts as you turn it. Your moods are not flaws but phases; each one shows a different lustre of the same true self.","Which of your moods have you been judging harshly, and what light might it be showing you?","a faceted quartz crystal catching starlight and splitting it into soft colour","clear-crystal"],
 ["the-sunbeam","The Sunbeam","sun","A sunbeam falls across the floor, and the dust drifting inside it turns to gold. Wherever your attention rests with love today, the ordinary will begin to shimmer.","What ordinary corner of your home or your day would shimmer if you looked at it with love?","an old wooden harp standing alone in a sunlit room","the-harp"],
 ["time-capsule","The Time Capsule","key","Somewhere ahead of you, a future self is opening the gift of today. Leave something worth finding: a kind word, a brave choice, a moment fully lived.","What would you like your future self to find when they look back on this ordinary week?","a folded letter sealed with red wax beside a quill and inkwell","sealed-letter"],
 ["the-veil","The Veil","lily","The veil between worlds grows thin in the quiet hours. You need not tear it aside; simply sit close, and what is meant for you will brush against your heart.","In which quiet moments do you feel nearest to something larger than yourself?","a candlelit stone chapel with open arched windows","sanctuary"],
 ["the-carousel","The Carousel","wheel","The carousel turns, and the painted horses rise and fall to the old music. Climb on for a round; joy does not need to go anywhere to be complete.","What simple pleasure have you been postponing until it could serve some useful purpose?","a wheel of the four seasons, spring blossom to winter frost around its rim","turning-wheel"],
 ["unopened-gift","The Unopened Gift","key","There is a gift in you still wrapped, waiting for its proper season. Do not shake it impatiently; the ribbon is already loosening on its own.","What talent or longing in you have you never fully unwrapped, and what might help it out into the light?","a golden key glowing on a velvet cushion","golden-key"],
 ["full-table","The Full Table","sun","Gather around the table you already have. Laughter, bread and good company are the oldest riches of all; count them tonight and feel how wealthy you are.","Who has sat at your table this year, and what has each of them brought into your life?","a fresh loaf of bread cooling on a wooden table beside a jug of milk","daily-bread"],
 ["bramble-rose","The Bramble Rose","flower","The wild rose grows where no one planted her and blooms anyway. You do not need permission to flourish; you need only keep turning towards the light.","Where are you waiting for a permission that no one is actually withholding from you?","a flowering hawthorn hedgerow alive with small birds along a country lane","the-hedgerow"],
 ["shell-echo","The Shell’s Echo","ship","Hold a shell to your ear and the ocean answers, though it lies miles away. What you long for is closer than distance suggests; listen for its echo within you.","What faraway longing can you already hear echoing, softly, through your daily life?","a cross-section of a nautilus shell showing its spiralling chambers","the-nautilus"],
 ["the-almanac","The Almanac","key","The old almanac knew when to sow, when to reap and when to rest. Your life keeps its own calendar; today is exactly the right day for whatever is ready.","What in your life is ready now, and what would be wiser left for its proper season?","a weathered stone sundial in a summer garden, its shadow falling across its face","the-sundial"],
 ["morning-glory","The Morning Glory","flower","The morning glory opens fully for a single day and holds nothing back. Give today your whole bloom; it is enough to be glorious once, and wholly.","What would it look like to hold nothing back from today, without worrying about tomorrow?","cherry blossoms drifting in spring light","the-blossom"],
 ["skylark","The Skylark","sun","The skylark climbs straight up into the open sky and sings the whole way, never waiting to arrive before it rejoices. Let your gladness rise with you today, not after.","What small joy could you let yourself sing about now, rather than saving it for when everything is finished?","birds singing in the trees as dawn breaks","dawn-chorus"],
 ["moon-halo","The Moon Halo","moon","Some nights the moon wears a pale ring of light, drawn from ice too high to see. Even your quietest hours may be crowned with something luminous you have not yet noticed.","What hidden grace has quietly encircled a difficult hour of yours, seen only when you looked again?","a solar eclipse with a glowing corona","the-eclipse"],
 ["kaleidoscope","The Kaleidoscope","crystal","Turn the glass a little and the same bright fragments fall into an entirely new pattern. Nothing in you needs replacing today; it only longs to be seen from a gentler angle.","Which familiar piece of your life might show a different beauty if you turned it slightly in the light?","curtains of the northern lights rippling over a snowy pine forest","the-aurora"],
 ["lovebirds","The Lovebirds","flower","Two small birds lean close upon one perch, preening each other’s feathers without hurry. Love lives in such tender, ordinary tending; offer it today, and let yourself be tended too.","How did someone care for you in a small way today, and how did you care for them in return?","an open ornate birdcage with a small bird perched on its threshold","the-birdcage"],
 ["slow-waltz","The Slow Waltz","wheel","In a waltz, one steps back so the other may step forward, and the turning belongs to both. Trust the rhythm between you and those you love; it is older and wiser than any single step.","Where in a close bond of yours might you lead a little less, or follow a little more gracefully?","two moons rising side by side over the sea","two-moons"],
 ["sandcastle","The Sandcastle","sun","The tide will come for the sandcastle, and the child builds it gladly all the same. Pour your whole heart into what is lovely now; its worth was never measured by how long it stands.","What did you give yourself to today simply for the joy of it, not for whether it would last?","the tide rolling back over a moonlit beach","returning-tide"],
 ["height-marks","The Height Marks","tree","Pencil lines climb the kitchen doorframe, each one dated in a loving hand. You are still growing, dear soul, in ways no ruler can measure, and someone has always been glad to notice.","Who first noticed how you were growing, and where have you grown this year without marking it?","an ancient arched door standing ajar with light beyond","open-door"],
 ["plaited-hair","The Plaited Hair","lily","Three strands, crossed patiently one over the other, become something stronger than any alone. So it is with the hands that raised you and the hands you now hold: woven, gentle, enduring.","Which threads of love, memory or kinship are woven most firmly through the person you have become?","a loom weaving golden threads into a tapestry of stars","the-weaver"],
 ["recipe-card","The Recipe Card","key","A stained card in a grandmother’s handwriting says only a pinch, a handful, until it looks right. Some wisdom is passed down to be felt rather than measured; trust what your hands already know.","What did those before you teach you without words, and how did you use that knowing today?","a fresh loaf of bread cooling on a wooden table beside a jug of milk","daily-bread"],
 ["rocking-horse","The Rocking Horse","star","In a corner of memory a painted horse still rocks, carrying a child to kingdoms only imagination could reach. That rider lives in you yet, and longs for one small adventure.","When did you last let the child in you play, dream or wander without needing a reason?","a wild horse galloping across moonlit plains","wild-horse"],
 ["faded-photograph","The Faded Photograph","eye","The colours have softened, yet every face in the old photograph still smiles towards you. Time gently blurs the edges of things but keeps their warmth; what you have loved is never wholly lost.","Which remembered face warmed you today, and what would you thank them for if they could hear you?","an ornate hand mirror reflecting a starry sky","the-mirror"],
 ["the-pawn","The Pawn","path","The smallest piece on the board moves one humble square at a time, yet it may cross the whole field and become a queen. Do not mistake a modest step for a small destiny.","What patient, unglamorous step did you take today that may be carrying you further than you know?","a turf labyrinth cut into a green hillside, seen from above at dusk","the-labyrinth"],
 ["mountain-ibex","The Mountain Ibex","path","The ibex stands calmly on ledges where others would never dare to tread, sure of its footing because it trusts its own body. You are steadier on the steep places than you believe.","Where did you find firm footing today in a situation that once would have made you tremble?","a winding trail up a mountain beneath the stars","the-mountain"],
 ["beacon-fire","The Beacon Fire","sun","Long ago, fires were lit from hilltop to hilltop to carry a single message across the land. Be brave enough to kindle your light, and you may find another answering from the next hill.","Whose light answered yours when you were brave, and who might be waiting for you to kindle first?","a phoenix rising in gold and flame","the-phoenix"],
 ["lamplighter","The Lamplighter","star","At dusk the lamplighter walks the lanes, lighting one lamp, then the next, never seeing the faces that pass beneath. Your quiet work brightens more paths than you will ever be shown.","Whose way might your ordinary work have made a little brighter today, even unseen?","a lantern held aloft in a dark forest","the-lantern"],
 ["dry-stone-wall","The Dry-Stone Wall","path","No mortar holds the dry-stone wall, only stones chosen with care and fitted to their neighbours, and still it stands for centuries. What you build patiently, piece by thoughtful piece, will hold.","Which careful piece of your work or life did you set in place today, and how well did it fit?","a worn wooden stile set in a dry-stone wall between two misty fields","the-stile"],
 ["the-wheelbarrow","The Wheelbarrow","wheel","The wheelbarrow asks nothing grand, only to carry one load across the garden and come back for the next. Honour the humble rounds of your labour; this is how gardens grow.","What simple, repeated task did you carry today, and what is slowly flourishing because of it?","an old straw beehive skep in a meadow, bees drifting among the clover","the-hive"],
 ["the-heartbeat","The Heartbeat","star","Lay a hand upon your chest and feel it: the drum that has kept faith with you through every day of your life, unasked. You are more faithfully loved, from within, than you know.","When today did you pause to feel your own aliveness, and what did your body seem to tell you?","a flame burning inside a crystal lantern","sacred-flame"],
 ["bare-feet","The Bare Feet","path","Slip off your shoes and let the cool grass and warm earth find the soles of your feet. The ground has always been ready to hold you; it only waits for you to arrive.","Where today did you feel truly held by the ground beneath you, and where might you seek it tomorrow?","a winding path climbing gently through hills toward a single bright star","open-path"],
 ["silver-scar","The Silver Scar","moon","The old wound has healed into a fine line of silver, catching the light like a thread of moonshine. Your body remembers what it survived, and wears it not as shame but as quiet grace.","Which mark on your body or your heart tells a story of healing you could honour tonight?","a lotus blooming from a dark pond","the-lotus"],
 ["the-hedgehog","The Hedgehog","moon","When the leaves fall, the hedgehog curls into a nest of them and sleeps until spring calls it out. There is no shame in drawing in; the deepest rest prepares the bravest waking.","Where in your life would a season of curling inward and resting serve you better than pressing on?","a pine cone opening its scales on a bed of forest moss","the-pinecone"],
 ["the-tortoise","The Tortoise","wheel","The tortoise carries its home upon its back and has never once been late for its own life. Go at the pace that is truly yours today; you arrive exactly when you are meant to.","Where did you rush today against your own natural pace, and what might unfold if you slowed?","a snail with a spiral shell climbing a dewy fern frond","the-snail"]
];
